WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.180 --> 00:00:03.000
- Jim Acosta was sitting 10 feet from me

00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:04.621
and he badmouthed me,

00:00:04.621 --> 00:00:09.621
saying a PR stunt that I
did, he blamed me directly,

00:00:09.730 --> 00:00:12.372
a PR stunt to get to promote MyPillow.

00:00:12.372 --> 00:00:14.955
(upbeat music)

00:00:21.560 --> 00:00:22.393
- I'm Dave Rubin

00:00:22.393 --> 00:00:24.860
and this is "The Rubin
Report Lockdown Edition."

00:00:24.860 --> 00:00:27.320
Remember everybody, you
can get all of our videos

00:00:27.320 --> 00:00:30.850
totally ad-free and
early at rubinreport.com.

00:00:30.850 --> 00:00:34.150
Joining me today is an American
businessman, entrepreneur,

00:00:34.150 --> 00:00:37.090
and founder and CEO of MyPillow.

00:00:37.090 --> 00:00:39.400
Mike Lindell, welcome
to "The Rubin Report."

00:00:39.400 --> 00:00:41.460
- Thanks for having me on.

00:00:41.460 --> 00:00:42.980
- Thanks for taking the time, my friend.

00:00:42.980 --> 00:00:45.350
I've wanted you on for quite some time,

00:00:45.350 --> 00:00:47.470
and then over the last couple of weeks

00:00:47.470 --> 00:00:49.730
you went from a guy
that's kind of hard to get

00:00:49.730 --> 00:00:52.150
to a guy that's impossibly hard to get,

00:00:52.150 --> 00:00:54.090
and now I've got you in a hotel

00:00:54.090 --> 00:00:56.520
and we're gonna take
advantage of the time.

00:00:56.520 --> 00:01:00.160
So everybody knows what
happened a couple weeks ago

00:01:00.160 --> 00:01:02.760
with you at the White
House and the brouhaha,

00:01:02.760 --> 00:01:05.430
and as I was saying to you off camera,

00:01:05.430 --> 00:01:08.310
watching the media go
after you was so consistent

00:01:08.310 --> 00:01:10.680
with what I've seen about
so many of my guests

00:01:10.680 --> 00:01:14.300
who have dared to take
an opposition opinion

00:01:14.300 --> 00:01:16.480
than mainstream allows for.

00:01:16.480 --> 00:01:18.070
But I want to hold that for a little bit

00:01:18.070 --> 00:01:20.040
because your backstory,

00:01:20.040 --> 00:01:22.890
what you've been through in
your life is pretty incredible

00:01:22.890 --> 00:01:27.280
and it's a true story of
perseverance actually.

00:01:27.280 --> 00:01:28.880
I know you've told the
story many times before,

00:01:28.880 --> 00:01:30.080
but could you just back us up

00:01:30.080 --> 00:01:32.650
and tell us the Mike Lindell story,

00:01:32.650 --> 00:01:35.960
and then we'll get to
everything happening in 2020.

00:01:35.960 --> 00:01:38.900
- Absolutely, and by
the way you talk about

00:01:38.900 --> 00:01:41.966
after I said that at the White
House, at the Rose Garden,

00:01:41.966 --> 00:01:44.280
I've had over 80
interviews now since then,

00:01:44.280 --> 00:01:46.710
so it's brought this platform

00:01:46.710 --> 00:01:49.171
that God's given me to just huge,

00:01:49.171 --> 00:01:50.630
and just when I think
it can't get any bigger,

00:01:50.630 --> 00:01:51.463
it gets bigger.

00:01:52.370 --> 00:01:56.450
You go all the way back for my story,

00:01:56.450 --> 00:01:59.077
it begins back, I guess, with my new book,

00:01:59.077 --> 00:02:01.870
"What Are the Odds? From
Crack Addict to CEO,"

00:02:01.870 --> 00:02:05.580
but it takes me back to
I was seven years old,

00:02:05.580 --> 00:02:07.320
my parents divorced,

00:02:07.320 --> 00:02:10.340
and that's when divorces weren't common.

00:02:10.340 --> 00:02:13.570
I got moved into a new
school two hours away,

00:02:13.570 --> 00:02:16.100
and I was the only kid in the whole school

00:02:16.100 --> 00:02:18.143
that was from a divorced family.

00:02:19.843 --> 00:02:21.810
I felt like right away
it started manifesting.

00:02:21.810 --> 00:02:23.073
I didn't fit in.

00:02:23.962 --> 00:02:24.850
I would do things,

00:02:24.850 --> 00:02:27.280
I remember climbing out
of a moving bus window

00:02:27.280 --> 00:02:30.570
to show off and jump into the ditch,

00:02:30.570 --> 00:02:32.640
we had snow in Minnesota luckily,

00:02:32.640 --> 00:02:34.817
and everyone, they would go,

00:02:34.817 --> 00:02:35.830
"Wow, can you believe he did that?"

00:02:35.830 --> 00:02:38.170
with these crazy things,

00:02:38.170 --> 00:02:39.420
or I wouldn't talk to them.

00:02:39.420 --> 00:02:41.980
I was very shy in that respect,

00:02:41.980 --> 00:02:43.750
but I thought in myself

00:02:43.750 --> 00:02:45.960
that there's something different about me.

00:02:45.960 --> 00:02:47.340
I just felt different.

00:02:47.340 --> 00:02:49.303
I didn't fit in with any one group,

00:02:50.537 --> 00:02:54.110
and this kept going on and
on throughout high school.

00:02:55.510 --> 00:02:57.960
If I'd go traveling
anywhere, if I'd be anywhere,

00:02:58.863 --> 00:03:02.230
I didn't even date really in
high school because of that.

00:03:02.230 --> 00:03:04.570
It was just this unworthiness spirit

00:03:04.570 --> 00:03:07.630
I think, when I look back now.

00:03:07.630 --> 00:03:09.430
I was at my five-year reunion,

00:03:09.430 --> 00:03:11.703
I worked the last two
jobs I had back then.

00:03:13.308 --> 00:03:15.270
I worked for someone, I
worked at a grocery store

00:03:15.270 --> 00:03:17.440
and a drive-in movie theater.

00:03:17.440 --> 00:03:18.590
If anybody out there
don't know what that is,

00:03:18.590 --> 00:03:21.030
it was a big theater where
you pulled up in our cars.

00:03:21.030 --> 00:03:22.950
(laughing)

00:03:22.950 --> 00:03:25.410
- I went to one drive-in
movie in my entire life.

00:03:25.410 --> 00:03:30.390
I saw "RoboCop" in about
1989 or so at a drive-in.

00:03:30.390 --> 00:03:32.620
- Yeah, it was a big thing
back when I was growing up.

00:03:32.620 --> 00:03:34.170
I worked there for seven years.

00:03:35.010 --> 00:03:37.370
It was voted the number one
place to work back then,

00:03:37.370 --> 00:03:41.760
by the way, if you were to work
for someone, and it was fun.

00:03:41.760 --> 00:03:44.330
But anyway, then I went
to college at the U of M

00:03:44.330 --> 00:03:47.050
and the first quarter I dropped out.

00:03:47.050 --> 00:03:48.840
I was still working the two jobs and that.

00:03:48.840 --> 00:03:49.983
I just dropped out.

00:03:51.190 --> 00:03:55.200
Right away, I was addicted
to compulsive gambling,

00:03:55.200 --> 00:03:57.330
and I started drinking about 17,

00:03:57.330 --> 00:03:59.923
actually late for 16 or 17.

00:04:02.450 --> 00:04:04.230
We got to our five-year reunion

00:04:04.230 --> 00:04:07.180
and I remember getting there,

00:04:07.180 --> 00:04:09.823
and of course I was probably
high and been drinking,

00:04:11.310 --> 00:04:16.310
and anyway all of these guys
had either started families,

00:04:16.320 --> 00:04:19.250
graduated from college,
started their careers,

00:04:19.250 --> 00:04:21.350
or they had kept the same job

00:04:21.350 --> 00:04:23.430
and moved up the corporate ladder already,

00:04:23.430 --> 00:04:25.060
so I was upset with myself

00:04:25.060 --> 00:04:28.430
that I wasn't where I knew I could be.

00:04:28.430 --> 00:04:29.560
Everybody was ahead of me.

00:04:29.560 --> 00:04:30.447
I thought, "Wow."

00:04:31.448 --> 00:04:33.690
But what I did is I took
over that whole reunion

00:04:33.690 --> 00:04:36.810
and told them about all
these stories that were true.

00:04:36.810 --> 00:04:39.310
I owed the mafia money, $20,000,

00:04:39.310 --> 00:04:42.960
they came to break my
arms for football bets.

00:04:42.960 --> 00:04:47.200
When I was 17, I got 18
tickets on a motorcycle

00:04:47.200 --> 00:04:49.023
in two days outrunning the cops.

00:04:50.090 --> 00:04:53.600
I went to go skydiving, fell
asleep on that motorcycle,

00:04:53.600 --> 00:04:57.560
crashed it, was bound and
determined, it was all banged up,

00:04:57.560 --> 00:05:01.060
and bound and determined to
get down to Stanton, Minnesota

00:05:01.060 --> 00:05:04.560
and finish this skydiving
jump, it was my ninth jump,

00:05:04.560 --> 00:05:06.350
and my parachute didn't open.

00:05:06.350 --> 00:05:09.140
I had a streamer, hit the
ground, and all these things,

00:05:09.140 --> 00:05:11.440
but I'm telling everyone at the reunion

00:05:11.440 --> 00:05:13.660
and they're just going, "Wow, wow."

00:05:13.660 --> 00:05:16.700
Well, I didn't hear
anything about anybody else,

00:05:16.700 --> 00:05:18.980
but I got home that
night and I laid in bed

00:05:18.980 --> 00:05:21.690
and it was just a deep
sadness came over me

00:05:21.690 --> 00:05:24.023
that I really wanted what they had,

00:05:24.890 --> 00:05:26.870
and I had fallen into this thing of like

00:05:26.870 --> 00:05:27.970
where's my life going?

00:05:30.840 --> 00:05:35.220
Well, then it was about 1982 or '83,

00:05:35.220 --> 00:05:36.053
you know, I did different things.

00:05:36.053 --> 00:05:39.810
Then I became a card counter,
a professional card counter.

00:05:39.810 --> 00:05:42.440
My uncle, I worked on
his farm raising pigs.

00:05:42.440 --> 00:05:44.900
I guess that was the last
job I had for someone,

00:05:44.900 --> 00:05:47.777
and I decided, "Well, I'm
gonna raise pigs myself.

00:05:47.777 --> 00:05:49.040
"Why am I working for him?"

00:05:49.040 --> 00:05:50.650
So I went and bought
all these feeder pigs,

00:05:50.650 --> 00:05:53.110
put them in a semi-residential area,

00:05:53.110 --> 00:05:55.850
and the bottom fell out of the market.

00:05:55.850 --> 00:05:57.123
That was a disaster.

00:05:58.496 --> 00:06:00.220
But I tried all these
entrepreneurial things

00:06:00.220 --> 00:06:04.330
on the same parallel track
as I had tried cocaine,

00:06:04.330 --> 00:06:06.940
and when I tried cocaine it was instant.

00:06:06.940 --> 00:06:08.210
I could be where I wanted to be.

00:06:08.210 --> 00:06:10.303
I had this false courage.

00:06:12.741 --> 00:06:14.030
It masked any pain I had.

00:06:14.030 --> 00:06:15.787
I felt like I was on top of the world.

00:06:15.787 --> 00:06:17.993
It didn't matter what
anybody thought of me.

00:06:19.317 --> 00:06:20.670
I felt better about myself.

00:06:20.670 --> 00:06:22.390
It was all these big lies,

00:06:22.390 --> 00:06:24.490
but I was a very functioning addict then,

00:06:24.490 --> 00:06:26.710
cocaine addict for 20 years,

00:06:26.710 --> 00:06:29.580
until I switched to
crack in the early 2000.

00:06:29.580 --> 00:06:33.680
But during that time, I
married the girl of my dreams,

00:06:33.680 --> 00:06:38.023
I had four kids, a very
functioning addict.

00:06:40.270 --> 00:06:41.460
Addiction affects everyone,

00:06:41.460 --> 00:06:43.250
no matter how many forks you eat with.

00:06:43.250 --> 00:06:45.520
People that say, "Oh, there
are addicts in the street,"

00:06:45.520 --> 00:06:47.490
that's what they perceive an addict at.

00:06:47.490 --> 00:06:50.400
Well, most of your
addicts, I hate to say it,

00:06:50.400 --> 00:06:52.800
are functioning, they're
in the corporate world.

00:06:54.220 --> 00:06:55.840
I was afraid of talking to anybody

00:06:55.840 --> 00:06:57.350
that had a suit and a tie on,

00:06:57.350 --> 00:06:59.620
I wasn't as good as them, you know.

00:06:59.620 --> 00:07:03.150
But they had just as many
problems as anybody does.

00:07:03.150 --> 00:07:08.100
Well, anyway, I was
always an entrepreneur.

00:07:08.100 --> 00:07:10.630
I ended up having a bar for 13 years,

00:07:10.630 --> 00:07:14.317
and that bar, probably a
bad place for an addict,

00:07:14.317 --> 00:07:17.480
but I tried different things in the bar.

00:07:17.480 --> 00:07:20.377
I learned a lot there with entertainment

00:07:20.377 --> 00:07:24.850
and advertising and
stuff, different things.

00:07:24.850 --> 00:07:26.960
A lot of the stuff I learned there,

00:07:26.960 --> 00:07:31.470
I learned the entrepreneurship,
I really took up,

00:07:31.470 --> 00:07:34.030
but it also was a bad
place for my addictions.

00:07:34.030 --> 00:07:37.000
Then it switched to
crack in the early 2000s,

00:07:37.000 --> 00:07:40.620
and then I could not do what I was doing

00:07:40.620 --> 00:07:43.640
with the bar anymore because
crack's a different drug.

00:07:43.640 --> 00:07:45.030
It's not a social drug.

00:07:45.030 --> 00:07:46.493
You're tweaking out windows.

00:07:48.130 --> 00:07:51.440
It took all my friends down
that were on crack very fast,

00:07:51.440 --> 00:07:53.150
and I said, "I'm never
gonna be like them,"

00:07:53.150 --> 00:07:55.310
and I ended up one of the worst ones,

00:07:55.310 --> 00:07:56.703
if there is such a thing.

00:07:59.676 --> 00:08:02.322
I had to sell the bar in 2003,

00:08:02.322 --> 00:08:05.270
and that was a circumstance
beyond my control,

00:08:05.270 --> 00:08:06.460
but it was going down anyway.

00:08:06.460 --> 00:08:08.823
It was going down the
back side with the crack.

00:08:11.020 --> 00:08:13.840
About 2004, in the middle
of the night one night,

00:08:13.840 --> 00:08:17.218
I had a dream of the name MyPillow.

00:08:17.218 --> 00:08:19.020
Now, I had always my
whole life searched for...

00:08:19.020 --> 00:08:20.080
I had problems with pillows.

00:08:20.080 --> 00:08:22.290
When I was 16 at that grocery store,

00:08:22.290 --> 00:08:25.340
I actually went out and took
one of my first paychecks

00:08:25.340 --> 00:08:28.827
and went out and looked
around at a department store

00:08:28.827 --> 00:08:32.655
and bought a $70 pillow in 1977.

00:08:32.655 --> 00:08:33.930
Who does that, right?

00:08:33.930 --> 00:08:36.900
- That's a seriously expensive pillow,

00:08:36.900 --> 00:08:38.100
adjusted for inflation.

00:08:38.100 --> 00:08:39.790
- Yeah, you adjust it,

00:08:39.790 --> 00:08:42.090
it was the most expensive
pillow I could find.

00:08:45.189 --> 00:08:46.850
What's strange that I'd
buy a pillow way back then

00:08:46.850 --> 00:08:47.683
to where I'm at now,

00:08:47.683 --> 00:08:51.100
but I tried it, it didn't
work, I couldn't return it,

00:08:51.100 --> 00:08:52.917
and I just remember that,

00:08:52.917 --> 00:08:55.110
but it was an endless search for pillows.

00:08:55.110 --> 00:08:58.650
Anyway, I had this dream
of MyPillow, the name,

00:08:58.650 --> 00:09:00.950
and I got up and I wrote
it all over the house,

00:09:00.950 --> 00:09:03.620
connecting the Y and the
P, and I'm all excited.

00:09:03.620 --> 00:09:05.330
One of my daughters comes upstairs

00:09:05.330 --> 00:09:06.780
about 2:00 in the morning,

00:09:06.780 --> 00:09:09.973
she's 11 or 12 years old, she
goes, "What are you doing?"

00:09:09.973 --> 00:09:11.217
I said, "I'm gonna invent this pillow.

00:09:11.217 --> 00:09:12.050
"It's gonna be called MyPillow.

00:09:12.050 --> 00:09:13.247
"What do you think of the name?

00:09:13.247 --> 00:09:14.877
"It's gonna change millions of people.

00:09:14.877 --> 00:09:17.227
"It's gonna be the biggest thing ever."

00:09:18.252 --> 00:09:19.776
I didn't even know what
was gonna be in it yet.

00:09:19.776 --> 00:09:20.610
(laughing)

00:09:20.610 --> 00:09:22.747
She grabs a glass of water and she goes,

00:09:22.747 --> 00:09:24.596
"That's really random, Dad."

00:09:24.596 --> 00:09:25.528
(Dave laughing)

00:09:25.528 --> 00:09:27.663
Then I went all in.

00:09:28.840 --> 00:09:31.180
I kept getting these dreams.

00:09:31.180 --> 00:09:34.490
What I wanted was
something you could adjust.

00:09:34.490 --> 00:09:36.690
Me and my one son, for day after day,

00:09:36.690 --> 00:09:39.520
he'd get home from
school and we would tear,

00:09:39.520 --> 00:09:42.440
I think we tried over 94
different kinds of foams

00:09:42.440 --> 00:09:43.680
and things to go in it.

00:09:43.680 --> 00:09:45.453
Nothing did what I wanted it to,

00:09:46.327 --> 00:09:48.400
but I just wouldn't give up on it.

00:09:48.400 --> 00:09:49.480
My friends were laughing.

00:09:49.480 --> 00:09:52.890
They're going, "Mike's gonna
invent a pillow, ha, ha, ha,"

00:09:52.890 --> 00:09:54.557
and the other ones would say,
"Hey, if you ever come up

00:09:54.557 --> 00:09:56.420
"with something like
that, I might want one."

00:09:56.420 --> 00:09:58.500
Well, it took about a
year, year and a half,

00:09:58.500 --> 00:10:00.163
and we finally had it done.

00:10:02.190 --> 00:10:04.603
We had no money left,
but we had some pillows.

00:10:05.440 --> 00:10:08.730
I took the first one, I went
into a Bed Bath &amp; Beyond,

00:10:08.730 --> 00:10:11.427
I remember going in there,
bringing it in and going,

00:10:11.427 --> 00:10:13.060
"Where's your manager?"

00:10:13.060 --> 00:10:14.257
They go, "He's over there."

00:10:14.257 --> 00:10:17.447
I'm talking to him, I go, "Hey,
I got the best pillow ever.

00:10:17.447 --> 00:10:19.120
"You can move it and it adjusts."

00:10:19.120 --> 00:10:20.770
I didn't really know everything.

00:10:20.770 --> 00:10:22.090
I said, "You can wash and dry it,"

00:10:22.090 --> 00:10:24.417
but I'm telling him all this
and I'm so passionate about it,

00:10:24.417 --> 00:10:25.250
"How many do you want?"

00:10:25.250 --> 00:10:27.700
I didn't know anything
about retailer selling.

00:10:27.700 --> 00:10:32.220
He goes, "We have one
buyer and he's not here."

00:10:32.220 --> 00:10:33.417
I go, "Well, where is he?"

00:10:33.417 --> 00:10:34.540
"Well, he's one national buyer."

00:10:34.540 --> 00:10:36.977
I was so persistent
and passionate he goes,

00:10:36.977 --> 00:10:38.870
"You need to leave now."

00:10:38.870 --> 00:10:40.727
I go, "No, really, how many do you want?"

00:10:40.727 --> 00:10:42.810
"Now." (laughing)

00:10:42.810 --> 00:10:45.760
This is the way it went,
closed door, one after another.

00:10:45.760 --> 00:10:49.530
Nobody wanted the pillow,
nobody wanted MyPillow.

00:10:49.530 --> 00:10:51.590
Someone said, "Mike, why
don't you do a kiosk?"

00:10:51.590 --> 00:10:53.413
I said, "How do you spell that?"

00:10:53.413 --> 00:10:54.590
(Dave laughing)

00:10:54.590 --> 00:10:56.200
I actually went to the kiosk

00:10:56.200 --> 00:10:57.800
and I found out something there.

00:10:57.800 --> 00:10:59.530
I was really out of my element

00:10:59.530 --> 00:11:03.733
because I could be on
drugs, selling or being,

00:11:04.705 --> 00:11:06.870
which one of the things too,
when I did sell a pillow

00:11:06.870 --> 00:11:10.880
all those times, I never broke
trust with the promoters.

00:11:10.880 --> 00:11:11.713
That's a key thing.

00:11:11.713 --> 00:11:14.050
But anyway, so we rented this kiosk

00:11:14.050 --> 00:11:17.380
in Eden Prairie, Minnesota,
and I couldn't stand it,

00:11:17.380 --> 00:11:19.260
talking to people straight.

00:11:19.260 --> 00:11:21.463
They'd come up and so it was just...

00:11:21.463 --> 00:11:25.020
I was shy, it was just
like I couldn't talk,

00:11:25.020 --> 00:11:28.080
and I'm actually hoping no
customers would come up.

00:11:28.080 --> 00:11:29.280
It was kind of weird.

00:11:29.280 --> 00:11:31.570
My wife at the time, she
worked most of the hours,

00:11:31.570 --> 00:11:32.790
but the one day I did work,

00:11:32.790 --> 00:11:35.070
the guy came up, very aggressive,

00:11:35.070 --> 00:11:37.990
he buys one, he says,
"You got a business card?"

00:11:37.990 --> 00:11:39.157
He said, "This is really unique.

00:11:39.157 --> 00:11:41.770
"You invented this, you
got a patent on it?"

00:11:41.770 --> 00:11:43.833
I said, "It's patent-pending."

00:11:45.250 --> 00:11:46.083
I said, "Oh, I'm all out,"

00:11:46.083 --> 00:11:49.603
and I wrote it on a piece of
paper, gave him my number.

00:11:50.540 --> 00:11:53.380
I remember the kiosk being such a failure

00:11:53.380 --> 00:11:57.970
and I ended up borrowing
money for Christmas presents.

00:11:57.970 --> 00:12:00.360
We had our house mortgaged,
we had nothing left,

00:12:00.360 --> 00:12:03.600
but we had 300 pillows and
that's all we had left.

00:12:03.600 --> 00:12:04.803
Everything was gone.

00:12:05.690 --> 00:12:09.137
That guy called around January
7th that year and he goes,

00:12:09.137 --> 00:12:11.200
"Are you the guy that invented
this pillow in Minnesota?"

00:12:11.200 --> 00:12:12.033
I said, "Yeah."

00:12:13.652 --> 00:12:15.640
And then I knew it, I knew I
only gave my number to one guy,

00:12:15.640 --> 00:12:18.807
and he goes, "Well, I run the
Minneapolis Home &amp; Garden Show

00:12:18.807 --> 00:12:21.367
"and I save a spot for
innovative products.

00:12:21.367 --> 00:12:25.590
"This pillow, I've been sleeping
on it, it changed my life."

00:12:25.590 --> 00:12:27.380
I'm going, "Wow."

00:12:27.380 --> 00:12:28.847
I said, "Yeah, I'll come in,"

00:12:28.847 --> 00:12:32.353
and I borrowed money to
actually get into his show.

00:12:33.320 --> 00:12:36.542
But I got in there, then I put a table up.

00:12:36.542 --> 00:12:39.660
I put a table out in front of me

00:12:39.660 --> 00:12:41.520
so the people could come in the booth,

00:12:41.520 --> 00:12:44.700
so I felt more secure,
like a security blanket,

00:12:44.700 --> 00:12:45.970
and they came by.

00:12:45.970 --> 00:12:48.290
That first day I remembered
I changed the booth

00:12:48.290 --> 00:12:49.780
and I did the selling,

00:12:49.780 --> 00:12:52.620
and it was easy for me then
because they were coming up

00:12:52.620 --> 00:12:53.880
and I had an agenda.

00:12:53.880 --> 00:12:57.090
I would tell them just X
amount, there was no smalltalk,

00:12:57.090 --> 00:12:59.200
and they would go by.

00:12:59.200 --> 00:13:01.410
Boy, I was selling them that first day,

00:13:01.410 --> 00:13:04.560
every single one of them
almost I think that first day.

00:13:04.560 --> 00:13:08.170
They came back the next day,
got back into the home show,

00:13:08.170 --> 00:13:11.813
and told me, came up and said,
"Wow, this pillow did this

00:13:11.813 --> 00:13:14.100
"and it helped me sleep," and all this.

00:13:14.100 --> 00:13:15.660
It wasn't about the money for me.

00:13:15.660 --> 00:13:18.480
For the first time, I felt so good inside

00:13:18.480 --> 00:13:20.630
that I had done something
to help somebody,

00:13:22.662 --> 00:13:24.420
and this ties in with
addiction and everything

00:13:24.420 --> 00:13:26.040
which I can tell you in a minute.

00:13:26.040 --> 00:13:29.980
But from that point on,
that started seven years

00:13:29.980 --> 00:13:34.300
of doing home shows and
fairs, going town-to-town

00:13:34.300 --> 00:13:37.440
throughout the Midwest,
then throughout the U.S.

00:13:37.440 --> 00:13:41.970
We'd make them and sell them
at these home shows and fairs,

00:13:41.970 --> 00:13:44.620
and just hours and hours of work.

00:13:44.620 --> 00:13:47.540
And some shows would be good,
some shows would be bad.

00:13:47.540 --> 00:13:52.540
But staying there on
track, with crack cocaine,

00:13:54.780 --> 00:13:55.723
another addiction.

00:13:57.108 --> 00:13:58.470
And then people were taking the company,

00:13:58.470 --> 00:14:00.210
there were so many that were attacking,

00:14:00.210 --> 00:14:02.580
trying to take the company,

00:14:02.580 --> 00:14:03.900
that we'd have someone work for us,

00:14:03.900 --> 00:14:06.970
there was different people, coming in,

00:14:06.970 --> 00:14:08.460
they'd seen something there.

00:14:08.460 --> 00:14:11.490
But I did get the patent.

00:14:11.490 --> 00:14:13.190
But they would copy, they
were trying to copy it

00:14:13.190 --> 00:14:14.120
and everything else.

00:14:14.120 --> 00:14:17.720
We ended up making
pillows, it got to be 2007,

00:14:17.720 --> 00:14:20.250
we were labeling them in our living room,

00:14:20.250 --> 00:14:22.927
and I'll never forget looking
over at my wife at the time

00:14:22.927 --> 00:14:25.620
and my son, one of my sons,

00:14:25.620 --> 00:14:27.600
and I knew that it had gotten so bad

00:14:27.600 --> 00:14:28.790
we were gonna lose everything

00:14:28.790 --> 00:14:32.143
'cause these guys were taking the company.

00:14:33.826 --> 00:14:35.550
The lights were gonna go out on the house,

00:14:35.550 --> 00:14:37.230
we were losing the house.

00:14:37.230 --> 00:14:40.170
And then my wife left about two days

00:14:40.170 --> 00:14:41.990
before the lights went out on the house.

00:14:41.990 --> 00:14:43.670
She couldn't take it anymore.

00:14:45.075 --> 00:14:47.980
So I went through, got a
divorce, lost everything there.

00:14:47.980 --> 00:14:50.823
The pillow was just a
little blip on the radar.

00:14:53.025 --> 00:14:55.410
And then it got to be 2008,

00:14:55.410 --> 00:14:58.223
and significant things happened in 2008,

00:14:58.223 --> 00:15:00.670
but the pillow company
was just like a pulse,

00:15:00.670 --> 00:15:03.180
like somebody in a coma.

00:15:03.180 --> 00:15:07.310
And one of the significant things,

00:15:07.310 --> 00:15:12.110
I was up 14 days with
no sleep in Minneapolis,

00:15:12.110 --> 00:15:13.240
and I come out of the room,

00:15:13.240 --> 00:15:15.150
and all three of the biggest drug dealers

00:15:15.150 --> 00:15:17.247
are standing there, and I
go, "What are you guys doing?

00:15:17.247 --> 00:15:18.080
"You know each other?"

00:15:18.080 --> 00:15:19.680
And they go, "We know of each other."

00:15:19.680 --> 00:15:22.197
And they said, "You've
been up for 14 days,

00:15:22.197 --> 00:15:24.160
"you're not getting any more crack."

00:15:24.160 --> 00:15:26.250
And I said, "Is this an intervention?"

00:15:26.250 --> 00:15:28.460
And the guy goes, "Call
it whatever you want."

00:15:28.460 --> 00:15:31.527
Well, two of them left,
and the other guy said,

00:15:31.527 --> 00:15:32.450
"How much you got left?"

00:15:32.450 --> 00:15:33.990
I showed him how much rocks.

00:15:33.990 --> 00:15:36.497
He sat down to make sure that
I did it and went to bed,

00:15:36.497 --> 00:15:37.830
wasn't getting any more.

00:15:37.830 --> 00:15:40.010
Well, he finally fell
sleep right about the time

00:15:40.010 --> 00:15:41.500
I was running out and I was tweaking

00:15:41.500 --> 00:15:44.530
and looking on the floor,
carpet colored farming,

00:15:44.530 --> 00:15:45.700
looking for crack.

00:15:45.700 --> 00:15:47.090
There never is crack there.

00:15:47.090 --> 00:15:49.410
Well, I went back downstairs,

00:15:49.410 --> 00:15:51.840
headed outside at 2:30 in the morning,

00:15:51.840 --> 00:15:55.300
and it's like bees in every
inner city in the country,

00:15:55.300 --> 00:15:57.540
you can get crack and you can get drugs.

00:15:57.540 --> 00:15:58.640
You're out there like bees.

00:15:58.640 --> 00:16:02.030
It's like a whole nother world.

00:16:02.030 --> 00:16:06.900
And I'm out there offering
money, $20 for a $5 rock.

00:16:06.900 --> 00:16:08.080
Nobody would take it.

00:16:08.080 --> 00:16:09.677
They're looking at me
like, "What are you, crazy?

00:16:09.677 --> 00:16:11.027
"We're not selling to you."

00:16:12.000 --> 00:16:13.840
They had threatened anyone on the street,

00:16:13.840 --> 00:16:16.320
if you sell to him, we're
gonna kill you, or who knows.

00:16:16.320 --> 00:16:19.457
Well, I came back upstairs
defeated, walked in there,

00:16:19.457 --> 00:16:21.397
and the dealer says, he says,

00:16:21.397 --> 00:16:23.170
"How'd that work out for you?"

00:16:23.170 --> 00:16:26.530
He says, "Give me your phone,
I'm gonna take a picture."

00:16:26.530 --> 00:16:28.627
And he took a picture, he
said, "There's for that book

00:16:28.627 --> 00:16:31.410
"you've been telling us about
you're gonna write someday."

00:16:31.410 --> 00:16:33.777
And he goes, "Man, you've
been telling us for years

00:16:33.777 --> 00:16:37.307
"that this MyPillow is
just a platform for God,

00:16:37.307 --> 00:16:39.187
"and you're gonna come back someday

00:16:39.187 --> 00:16:40.507
"and you're gonna help us all out

00:16:40.507 --> 00:16:42.827
"of this addiction world that we live in,

00:16:42.827 --> 00:16:45.060
"and we're not gonna let you die on us."

00:16:45.060 --> 00:16:47.980
I was their hope, 'cause I
told them that all the time.

00:16:47.980 --> 00:16:50.520
Here's the actual on my
book, the actual picture.

00:16:50.520 --> 00:16:51.830
It goes into a hologram.

00:16:51.830 --> 00:16:53.640
You see the bad picture there?

00:16:53.640 --> 00:16:55.160
- [Dave] Unbelievable, unbelievable.

00:16:55.160 --> 00:16:57.520
- I put that on there,
so that was the picture

00:16:57.520 --> 00:17:00.883
taken in 2008, and then to where I am now.

00:17:02.580 --> 00:17:04.660
And by the way, two of
those guys work for me now.

00:17:04.660 --> 00:17:07.970
They're born-again Christians
and none of them sell anymore.

00:17:07.970 --> 00:17:09.970
So it's come full circle.

00:17:09.970 --> 00:17:13.693
But that year, my son was
crying in the driveway.

00:17:14.700 --> 00:17:15.860
He had got back from a hunting trip.

00:17:15.860 --> 00:17:18.930
He's all teared up, he was 18, he said,

00:17:18.930 --> 00:17:20.700
this was another place
where you're in a losing...

00:17:20.700 --> 00:17:22.441
I said, "You coming in?"

00:17:22.441 --> 00:17:25.010
He goes, "No, dad, I
can't live here anymore."

00:17:25.010 --> 00:17:27.440
I thought I was hiding it from him.

00:17:27.440 --> 00:17:29.610
And I just said, I'm quivering

00:17:29.610 --> 00:17:30.910
'cause it's breaking my heart,

00:17:30.910 --> 00:17:34.030
and I said, "Yeah, you can
go live with your brother,

00:17:34.030 --> 00:17:35.240
that's no problem."

00:17:35.240 --> 00:17:38.830
And it just hit me, like you
ain't hiding it from anybody.

00:17:38.830 --> 00:17:43.280
And then this guy came in December,

00:17:43.280 --> 00:17:47.190
this is really key to my
Lindell Recovery Network

00:17:47.190 --> 00:17:49.020
when we talk in a minute,

00:17:49.020 --> 00:17:51.000
my friend came in December.

00:17:51.000 --> 00:17:52.520
There was nothing left.

00:17:52.520 --> 00:17:55.073
I was sitting in the
house, everything was gone.

00:17:57.830 --> 00:17:58.850
Dick comes walking in.

00:17:58.850 --> 00:18:00.280
I go, "Dick, what are you going here?"

00:18:00.280 --> 00:18:02.650
Now he was my equal, we were the same age,

00:18:02.650 --> 00:18:04.810
we both started cocaine at the same time,

00:18:04.810 --> 00:18:07.630
very functioning addicts,
both switched to crack

00:18:07.630 --> 00:18:10.880
about the same time, and he
had quit four years earlier

00:18:10.880 --> 00:18:12.160
and found the Lord.

00:18:12.160 --> 00:18:15.387
And I heard about that,
but here he shows up,

00:18:15.387 --> 00:18:17.160
and I go, "Dick, what are you doing?"

00:18:17.160 --> 00:18:18.670
And he goes, "The Lord led me here."

00:18:18.670 --> 00:18:20.120
He goes, "What's going on?"

00:18:20.120 --> 00:18:21.357
I go, "Well, as long as you're here,

00:18:21.357 --> 00:18:23.280
"I got questions for you."

00:18:23.280 --> 00:18:25.170
I said, "First of all, is it boring?"

00:18:25.170 --> 00:18:27.010
He goes, "No, man, it ain't boring."

00:18:27.010 --> 00:18:29.040
And I drilled him for an hour.

00:18:29.040 --> 00:18:31.880
I drilled him for an hour,
because you know what?

00:18:31.880 --> 00:18:35.460
I respected his answers because
he's been where I'd been

00:18:35.460 --> 00:18:38.280
and he had made it through somehow.

00:18:38.280 --> 00:18:40.570
I call it my hope match in my book.

00:18:40.570 --> 00:18:43.070
Well, a month later, I end up quitting.

00:18:43.070 --> 00:18:47.120
On January 16, 2009, I prayed
and I said, "Okay, God."

00:18:47.120 --> 00:18:48.400
There was nothing left.

00:18:48.400 --> 00:18:50.640
I made sure I didn't have
any money or anything

00:18:50.640 --> 00:18:53.040
so they say it was at your bottom.

00:18:53.040 --> 00:18:54.452
It wasn't really my bottom.

00:18:54.452 --> 00:18:56.750
I think I could have
survived without money,

00:18:56.750 --> 00:19:00.150
but I knew if I went one more day,

00:19:00.150 --> 00:19:02.170
I would have two courses on my life.

00:19:02.170 --> 00:19:04.840
One would be my calling,
where I'm at today,

00:19:04.840 --> 00:19:07.760
and if I went one more
day, that would be gone.

00:19:07.760 --> 00:19:09.923
It would be whatever reel B would be like,

00:19:09.923 --> 00:19:12.750
like an old drive-in, whatever
the second feature would be,

00:19:12.750 --> 00:19:14.910
wherever that path was taking me,

00:19:14.910 --> 00:19:17.010
that's where that was going.

00:19:17.010 --> 00:19:19.617
So I prayed, I said, "I'm
gonna wake up in the morning

00:19:19.617 --> 00:19:22.200
"and never have the desire again."

00:19:22.200 --> 00:19:25.490
And I woke up in the morning,
and all the desires were gone.

00:19:25.490 --> 00:19:28.710
Now, I did go to a faith-based
center about two months later

00:19:28.710 --> 00:19:31.150
to find out why I was an
addict in the first place,

00:19:31.150 --> 00:19:35.492
but then things started
happening, that these miracles...

00:19:35.492 --> 00:19:38.240
These guys had taken the
company and took all my shows,

00:19:38.240 --> 00:19:40.163
and I needed $30,000.

00:19:43.895 --> 00:19:47.227
I met this guy, this is just
a story I tell all the time,

00:19:48.220 --> 00:19:50.337
this guy said, "Oh, I have
some guys that'll take a chance

00:19:50.337 --> 00:19:51.360
"and borrow money or whatever,"

00:19:51.360 --> 00:19:53.510
and I talked to him a
couple weeks earlier.

00:19:55.190 --> 00:19:57.680
I meant to meet him, I needed
the money, in the afternoon,

00:19:57.680 --> 00:20:01.030
30 grand, and I was walking
in there with a tee-shirt,

00:20:01.030 --> 00:20:04.140
and here I walk in, and I don't
know these guys from Adam,

00:20:04.140 --> 00:20:08.190
here's a CIO, a CIEO, a CFO,
they're all wearing suits.

00:20:08.190 --> 00:20:09.520
I'm scared to death.

00:20:09.520 --> 00:20:11.257
I go in there with a pillow, and I go,

00:20:11.257 --> 00:20:12.947
"Hey, you guys, I wanna borrow 30 grand.

00:20:12.947 --> 00:20:15.077
"I'll pay you back 40
grand within two months.

00:20:15.077 --> 00:20:16.387
"I'm gonna set up shows.

00:20:16.387 --> 00:20:17.377
"I'm gonna have the biggest,

00:20:17.377 --> 00:20:19.867
"it's gonna be the biggest
company in the world someday.

00:20:19.867 --> 00:20:21.327
"These guys took my company.

00:20:21.327 --> 00:20:22.960
"I used to be a crack cocaine addict."

00:20:22.960 --> 00:20:25.017
And one of the guys said,
the CFO I think it was,

00:20:25.017 --> 00:20:26.630
"Well, when did you quit crack?"

00:20:26.630 --> 00:20:28.259
And I said, "Last Thursday."

00:20:28.259 --> 00:20:29.290
(laughing)

00:20:29.290 --> 00:20:32.080
Literally, four of them
got up and left the room,

00:20:32.080 --> 00:20:34.830
and it's like "Shark Tank,"
for that reason, we're out.

00:20:35.848 --> 00:20:38.730
And the other four ended
up giving me the money.

00:20:38.730 --> 00:20:40.283
- Wow.
- They got zapped.

00:20:43.370 --> 00:20:45.210
They never checked my
ID, 'cause I knew that,

00:20:45.210 --> 00:20:46.710
'cause I didn't have a driver's license.

00:20:46.710 --> 00:20:49.250
So I walked out of there with the cash,

00:20:49.250 --> 00:20:50.190
ended up paying them back,

00:20:50.190 --> 00:20:53.610
but things like that kept
happening for the next two years.

00:20:53.610 --> 00:20:56.360
I got up to when I did that, I
said to my friends and family

00:20:56.360 --> 00:20:59.367
we had no money left again, and I said,

00:20:59.367 --> 00:21:00.727
"You guys, if we all put in money,

00:21:00.727 --> 00:21:03.167
"I have a dream of the
biggest infomercial ever."

00:21:03.167 --> 00:21:06.720
"If no box store is gonna take
us, nobody's gonna take us."

00:21:06.720 --> 00:21:09.390
Because everybody that bought
it at those shows loved it,

00:21:09.390 --> 00:21:11.353
and people would tell other people.

00:21:12.900 --> 00:21:13.733
So they put their money in,

00:21:13.733 --> 00:21:17.287
and we were told by these
professionals, going,

00:21:17.287 --> 00:21:18.917
"Oh, infomercials don't work.

00:21:18.917 --> 00:21:21.270
"It's just to get into the box stores."

00:21:21.270 --> 00:21:23.017
I said, "Well, the box
stores don't want me,

00:21:23.017 --> 00:21:24.097
"and I don't wanna go there.

00:21:24.097 --> 00:21:25.250
"I'm gonna do it my way."

00:21:25.250 --> 00:21:27.410
And they said, "Oh, it won't
work, you need an actor."

00:21:27.410 --> 00:21:29.627
And I said, "I wanna do it
like I did at the shows,

00:21:29.627 --> 00:21:32.320
"with a real audience, make things real."

00:21:32.320 --> 00:21:37.280
The infomercial launched at
3:00 a.m. on October 7, 2011.

00:21:37.280 --> 00:21:39.610
I was living in my sister's basement.

00:21:39.610 --> 00:21:43.480
Everything I had was
banked on that infomercial.

00:21:43.480 --> 00:21:46.100
And it aired, and I had 10 employees.

00:21:46.100 --> 00:21:48.680
Now we had just phones
that we were taking,

00:21:48.680 --> 00:21:51.800
everybody taking phones
up, my friends or whatever,

00:21:51.800 --> 00:21:55.890
and within 40 days we had 500 employees.

00:21:55.890 --> 00:21:57.530
It just exploded.

00:21:57.530 --> 00:21:59.160
I built my own call center.

00:21:59.160 --> 00:22:00.980
We were hiring people off the street.

00:22:00.980 --> 00:22:02.610
They go, "Mike, you need to be CEO."

00:22:02.610 --> 00:22:04.187
I go, "Why do I need to be CEO?

00:22:04.187 --> 00:22:05.310
"Let's make pillows."

00:22:05.310 --> 00:22:06.720
They go, "We need an HR department."

00:22:06.720 --> 00:22:07.837
I go, "That sounds horrible."

00:22:07.837 --> 00:22:09.120
"We need a corporate attorney."

00:22:09.120 --> 00:22:10.730
I said, "That's even worse."
(Dave laughing)

00:22:10.730 --> 00:22:13.638
And we never missed a
beat, we never missed a...

00:22:13.638 --> 00:22:15.707
Everybody got their pillows on time,

00:22:15.707 --> 00:22:17.840
MyPillows on time for Christmas.

00:22:17.840 --> 00:22:19.390
But it just went (blowing air).

00:22:20.740 --> 00:22:22.670
- All right, there's so much there,

00:22:22.670 --> 00:22:25.230
but I wanna focus a little bit on the fact

00:22:25.230 --> 00:22:28.810
that it seems like you found your purpose

00:22:28.810 --> 00:22:33.080
in the midst of on absolutely
chaotic time in your life,

00:22:33.080 --> 00:22:35.020
sounds like personally, family,

00:22:35.020 --> 00:22:37.240
obviously the drugs and the rest of it.

00:22:37.240 --> 00:22:40.490
When you look back now,
do you think you needed

00:22:40.490 --> 00:22:44.020
all of that craziness to
actually find the purpose

00:22:44.020 --> 00:22:46.380
that now is clearly
having you live the life

00:22:46.380 --> 00:22:47.213
you're supposed to be living?

00:22:47.213 --> 00:22:48.760
- Well, absolutely.

00:22:48.760 --> 00:22:52.600
You see me wear my cross
on TV all the time,

00:22:52.600 --> 00:22:55.023
and I even wear it when
I didn't have it on TV.

00:22:56.420 --> 00:22:58.770
I would always tell my
friends after the bar closed

00:22:58.770 --> 00:23:00.667
back in the day, I would tell them about,

00:23:00.667 --> 00:23:02.647
"Hey, I read about Revelation in the Bible

00:23:02.647 --> 00:23:04.000
"when I was in jail."

00:23:04.000 --> 00:23:05.620
I'd be witnessing to them.

00:23:05.620 --> 00:23:08.730
I didn't have God or the
Lord, a personal relationship.

00:23:08.730 --> 00:23:10.460
Those guys would quit that day.

00:23:10.460 --> 00:23:12.580
28 people quit during those years,

00:23:12.580 --> 00:23:15.157
and my friends are going,
"What are you saying to them?

00:23:15.157 --> 00:23:16.480
"We're losing friends."

00:23:16.480 --> 00:23:18.890
Well, it was all those times,

00:23:18.890 --> 00:23:21.600
'cause I had 14 near-death experiences

00:23:21.600 --> 00:23:23.140
that would run through my book.

00:23:23.140 --> 00:23:25.223
I had things that only you go,

00:23:25.223 --> 00:23:27.160
that in the book it's
like what are the odds?

00:23:27.160 --> 00:23:28.850
When you have a one in a million happen,

00:23:28.850 --> 00:23:33.500
a one in a billion, or you
push this off just to chance,

00:23:33.500 --> 00:23:35.420
when you add them up in your own lives,

00:23:35.420 --> 00:23:37.040
when does it become a miracle?

00:23:37.040 --> 00:23:41.810
For me, I used mathematical
odds that God has to be real

00:23:41.810 --> 00:23:46.810
because all the stuff that
happened to me was impossible.

00:23:47.530 --> 00:23:50.339
My actual day that I did a
full surrender, get this,

00:23:50.339 --> 00:23:51.821
(phone ringing)

00:23:51.821 --> 00:23:53.763
it was February 18, 2017.

00:23:58.363 --> 00:23:59.970
That's just a few years ago.

00:23:59.970 --> 00:24:04.310
But I always had faith,
but I didn't have...

00:24:04.310 --> 00:24:07.500
To answer your question,
everything that happened to me,

00:24:07.500 --> 00:24:11.110
I say it all the time, I
would not change one thing

00:24:11.110 --> 00:24:13.100
if it's not where I'm at right now,

00:24:13.100 --> 00:24:16.660
because that convinced
me that God was real,

00:24:16.660 --> 00:24:18.720
and I just turned it over
to him full surrender,

00:24:18.720 --> 00:24:21.550
and now I can go out and use my platform.

00:24:21.550 --> 00:24:26.070
I don't have any worries,
I put all my faith in God,

00:24:26.070 --> 00:24:28.840
and I can go out and do these things,

00:24:28.840 --> 00:24:31.930
my evangelism, things to help people.

00:24:31.930 --> 00:24:32.820
That's what I do.

00:24:32.820 --> 00:24:34.880
This wasn't about selling a pillow.

00:24:34.880 --> 00:24:38.043
It always has been MyPillow was
the platform, and that's it.

00:24:39.010 --> 00:24:41.500
- You must have had
people from the outside,

00:24:41.500 --> 00:24:44.160
probably lawyers, PR
people, the rest of it,

00:24:44.160 --> 00:24:45.637
that must have been saying to you,

00:24:45.637 --> 00:24:47.587
"Mike, the pillow is great and all,

00:24:47.587 --> 00:24:48.537
"you can keep selling them,

00:24:48.537 --> 00:24:51.407
"but you probably shouldn't
talk about the story that much,

00:24:51.407 --> 00:24:53.700
"the crack that much, religion that much,"

00:24:53.700 --> 00:24:56.450
the other things that clearly
are the drivers behind you.

00:24:56.450 --> 00:24:58.790
But did you just ignore
those voices all the time?

00:24:58.790 --> 00:25:00.490
And I'm sure you still hear them now.

00:25:00.490 --> 00:25:03.710
- Yeah, here's a good one,
this first started happening

00:25:03.710 --> 00:25:05.800
when I wore my cross on TV.

00:25:05.800 --> 00:25:08.760
I was up in Canada on a shopping channel,

00:25:08.760 --> 00:25:12.502
and I was all by myself,
all lonely or whatever,

00:25:12.502 --> 00:25:15.190
and it was just like I said, I
still had that thing going on

00:25:15.190 --> 00:25:16.410
where I couldn't talk to people

00:25:16.410 --> 00:25:19.360
and I'd rather be alone at that time.

00:25:19.360 --> 00:25:22.220
Anyway, I was breaking
every record they ever had,

00:25:22.220 --> 00:25:25.307
and all of a sudden, here's
somebody, a lady shows up,

00:25:25.307 --> 00:25:27.900
and this is a 24-hour
thing, it's grueling.

00:25:27.900 --> 00:25:30.010
You get to sleep for like five hours.

00:25:30.010 --> 00:25:32.287
She walks in my room and she goes,

00:25:32.287 --> 00:25:34.457
"Hello, I'm your executive producer,

00:25:34.457 --> 00:25:36.767
"and congratulations,
you've broken every record

00:25:36.767 --> 00:25:39.987
"here in Canada, but I
need you to take your cross

00:25:39.987 --> 00:25:43.017
"and tuck it in your shirt or take it off

00:25:43.017 --> 00:25:45.080
"for the rest of the time you're here."

00:25:45.080 --> 00:25:47.430
And I looked at her and I
said, "And why is that?"

00:25:47.430 --> 00:25:48.687
And she goes, "That's religious,

00:25:48.687 --> 00:25:51.637
"prejudice against other
religions," or something like that.

00:25:51.637 --> 00:25:53.960
And I just went on a rant.

00:25:53.960 --> 00:25:56.181
I still had a little anger issues then,

00:25:56.181 --> 00:25:59.550
and I just flipped out, 'cause
I wanted to leave anyway.

00:25:59.550 --> 00:26:01.810
It was like the movie, "My Cousin Vinny,"

00:26:01.810 --> 00:26:04.352
when the gal wants to say,
"You're right, goodbye."

00:26:04.352 --> 00:26:06.250
(Dave laughing)

00:26:06.250 --> 00:26:08.100
I go, "You're right, I'm outta here."

00:26:08.959 --> 00:26:10.597
I said, "That cross is staying there,

00:26:10.597 --> 00:26:12.450
"so either you like it or not."

00:26:12.450 --> 00:26:14.587
And she stopped and she goes,

00:26:14.587 --> 00:26:17.047
"Well, if you feel that strongly about it,

00:26:17.047 --> 00:26:18.707
"I guess you can leave it on."

00:26:19.804 --> 00:26:21.550
This is the thing I fought with that,

00:26:21.550 --> 00:26:24.500
people used to call me
when I was the only person

00:26:24.500 --> 00:26:26.980
taking phone calls, doing
them home shows and stuff,

00:26:26.980 --> 00:26:29.730
and I did a little
public access TV station,

00:26:29.730 --> 00:26:31.667
and people would call up and say,

00:26:31.667 --> 00:26:35.110
"You're wearing your cross on
TV," and they'd be atheist,

00:26:35.110 --> 00:26:37.560
they'd even be Christians
slamming me for it.

00:26:37.560 --> 00:26:38.603
It didn't matter.

00:26:39.490 --> 00:26:40.610
I would argue with them.

00:26:40.610 --> 00:26:42.520
It wasn't about selling a pillow then.

00:26:42.520 --> 00:26:45.110
I'm arguing with them and telling them

00:26:45.110 --> 00:26:47.883
things in the Bible again and
things that happened to me

00:26:47.883 --> 00:26:50.640
that couldn't have been
any other explanation.

00:26:50.640 --> 00:26:52.273
They would find Jesus and hang up,

00:26:52.273 --> 00:26:54.850
and I'd go, "Take that,
how do you like me now?"

00:26:54.850 --> 00:26:56.234
And I'm still unsaved.

00:26:56.234 --> 00:26:59.129
(laughing)

00:26:59.129 --> 00:27:01.190
And then it manifested, it's funny,

00:27:01.190 --> 00:27:03.060
I'll skip ahead, I gotta tell you this,

00:27:03.060 --> 00:27:05.250
now when they say boycott Mike Lindell

00:27:05.250 --> 00:27:08.470
and boycott MyPillow on the
trolls and bots on Twitter,

00:27:08.470 --> 00:27:10.337
the other people say all the time,

00:27:10.337 --> 00:27:11.980
"Don't boycott him."

00:27:11.980 --> 00:27:13.277
He goes, "He'll double his ads.

00:27:13.277 --> 00:27:15.103
"We see enough of that guy."

00:27:15.103 --> 00:27:16.530
(laughing)

00:27:16.530 --> 00:27:18.630
- When we get in a little
bit to what happened to you

00:27:18.630 --> 00:27:21.860
after the Rose Garden speech,
that was an interesting moment

00:27:21.860 --> 00:27:23.840
because I saw a ton of that.

00:27:23.840 --> 00:27:25.150
The media's going after you,

00:27:25.150 --> 00:27:27.100
and then you look at what
regular people are saying

00:27:27.100 --> 00:27:28.517
and they're like, "Yeah,
I just bought a pillow,

00:27:28.517 --> 00:27:29.760
"I just bought a pillow."

00:27:29.760 --> 00:27:32.030
People are screenshotting
receipts and the rest of it.

00:27:32.030 --> 00:27:34.100
But I wanna talk a little bit more

00:27:34.100 --> 00:27:35.570
about the business specifically,

00:27:35.570 --> 00:27:39.960
because the idea that you
did the on-air infomercials

00:27:39.960 --> 00:27:42.130
and that sort of thing,
and that you still do them,

00:27:42.130 --> 00:27:45.080
it's like there's something about them.

00:27:45.080 --> 00:27:47.210
The amount of times that I've
watched your infomercials,

00:27:47.210 --> 00:27:49.997
or I remember growing
up watching Ron Popeil,

00:27:49.997 --> 00:27:51.710
"Set it and forget it,"

00:27:51.710 --> 00:27:54.180
all of those things, that spray hair.

00:27:54.180 --> 00:27:57.750
For some reason, even if you
weren't gonna buy those things,

00:27:57.750 --> 00:27:58.640
you watched them.

00:27:58.640 --> 00:28:00.950
There was something about them.

00:28:00.950 --> 00:28:03.340
Do you think there is some
sort of magic to that,

00:28:03.340 --> 00:28:06.063
beyond just being yourself
or whatever Ron had?

00:28:06.987 --> 00:28:07.820
What is it about them?

00:28:07.820 --> 00:28:10.130
- I think God's given me this platform,

00:28:10.130 --> 00:28:15.130
and for me, for my gift from
God, to be able to speak

00:28:15.440 --> 00:28:18.363
and to have that, that's
my calling to be that.

00:28:19.333 --> 00:28:21.220
That's beyond anything I'd ever imagined.

00:28:21.220 --> 00:28:23.710
But one of the things
is we make them real.

00:28:23.710 --> 00:28:25.110
We do all our own commercials.

00:28:25.110 --> 00:28:27.410
We have other companies,
we tell them what to do.

00:28:27.410 --> 00:28:29.810
It's just me and a couple of
my people inside MyPillow.

00:28:29.810 --> 00:28:33.850
We make them real, and it's an anomaly.

00:28:33.850 --> 00:28:37.450
No products have made
it sustainable on TV.

00:28:37.450 --> 00:28:40.120
Every time you see a MyPillow,
it either breaks even,

00:28:40.120 --> 00:28:42.700
that one, exact one, either breaks even

00:28:42.700 --> 00:28:44.000
or makes a little bit,

00:28:44.000 --> 00:28:46.350
'cause I don't need the
other stores and stuff.

00:28:47.664 --> 00:28:49.130
I did something that's
never been done before

00:28:49.130 --> 00:28:52.180
where you're directly to the consumer,

00:28:52.180 --> 00:28:55.113
directly to the public.

00:28:56.640 --> 00:29:01.270
One of the things is I think
it's the realness of it,

00:29:01.270 --> 00:29:05.730
and I've been on TV now 2.8 million times.

00:29:05.730 --> 00:29:07.670
I heard that number, I
had to fact-check it.

00:29:07.670 --> 00:29:09.047
I'm going, "What?"

00:29:11.550 --> 00:29:13.510
To me, it's beyond
anything I've ever seen.

00:29:13.510 --> 00:29:18.510
But once again, that platform,
to get that platform of trust

00:29:19.050 --> 00:29:24.050
and of realness, it's
just this is who I am

00:29:24.870 --> 00:29:26.400
and I'm not gonna change,

00:29:26.400 --> 00:29:28.050
and I'm putting it right out there.

00:29:28.050 --> 00:29:30.540
That's why you won't see
one of my commercials

00:29:30.540 --> 00:29:32.027
where I'm not wearing that cross,

00:29:32.027 --> 00:29:36.290
and people like to see what's
real, and it transfers over.

00:29:36.290 --> 00:29:38.000
I am who you see on TV.

00:29:38.000 --> 00:29:40.790
I'm not something different
that's all canned.

00:29:40.790 --> 00:29:43.300
Most of the things you
see, like the one back in,

00:29:43.300 --> 00:29:46.120
the man in the mirror
one time over by the bed,

00:29:46.120 --> 00:29:49.610
we had one whole day of
taping where I'm over there

00:29:49.610 --> 00:29:52.743
with that couple in the man in
the mirror, that commercial,

00:29:53.870 --> 00:29:55.487
and I'm holding it, and I go,

00:29:55.487 --> 00:29:57.480
"You're gonna wake up in the
morning and (screeching)."

00:29:57.480 --> 00:29:59.449
We just left that natural stuff in there,

00:29:59.449 --> 00:30:00.666
and people would see me on the streets,

00:30:00.666 --> 00:30:01.689
and they'd go (screeching).

00:30:01.689 --> 00:30:03.939
(laughing)

00:30:06.437 --> 00:30:09.180
The jingle's so powerful,
too, that was cool.

00:30:09.180 --> 00:30:10.560
- Well, it's just so obvious also

00:30:10.560 --> 00:30:11.570
that you were ahead of the curve,

00:30:11.570 --> 00:30:13.480
because now because of podcasts

00:30:13.480 --> 00:30:14.510
and YouTube and everything else,

00:30:14.510 --> 00:30:16.500
almost everything in the digital space

00:30:16.500 --> 00:30:18.380
is direct to consumer, right?

00:30:18.380 --> 00:30:21.910
Everybody's often using code
Rubin or whatever it might be

00:30:21.910 --> 00:30:23.000
to sell their products.

00:30:23.000 --> 00:30:25.850
So you, through going deep on television,

00:30:25.850 --> 00:30:27.290
you actually helped model something

00:30:27.290 --> 00:30:29.640
that now really works online, too.

00:30:29.640 --> 00:30:33.660
- Well, it depends what
you pay for the online.

00:30:33.660 --> 00:30:35.713
It's just like a TV ad on TV.

00:30:37.459 --> 00:30:38.750
I'm very blessed all of a sudden

00:30:38.750 --> 00:30:42.360
that I could never put any ads on CNN.

00:30:42.360 --> 00:30:43.790
I'll say this straight up.

00:30:43.790 --> 00:30:44.990
I couldn't put any ads there

00:30:44.990 --> 00:30:47.880
because they were still
charging for a bigger viewership

00:30:47.880 --> 00:30:50.950
from back in the day, so it
didn't matter what I did.

00:30:50.950 --> 00:30:53.730
But just recently, I was
able to break even on them,

00:30:53.730 --> 00:30:54.567
so I'm putting them right...

00:30:54.567 --> 00:30:57.297
And here I got of their hosts
saying bad things about me,

00:30:57.297 --> 00:30:59.301
and all of a sudden my
commercial comes up,

00:30:59.301 --> 00:31:01.580
hello, I'm Mike Lindell,
how are you doing,

00:31:01.580 --> 00:31:03.483
wearing my cross, and there you go.

00:31:04.660 --> 00:31:06.260
That's pretty cool.

00:31:06.260 --> 00:31:07.890
- That's about as good as it gets.

00:31:07.890 --> 00:31:10.690
Okay, so let's talk about the CNN host

00:31:10.690 --> 00:31:12.370
and what happened over
the last couple of weeks.

00:31:12.370 --> 00:31:15.930
So obviously, we're in
the middle of coronavirus,

00:31:15.930 --> 00:31:18.300
President Trump gives a
speech at the Rose Garden,

00:31:18.300 --> 00:31:20.860
updating people on what's going on,

00:31:20.860 --> 00:31:23.410
as he's been doing pretty much every day,

00:31:23.410 --> 00:31:25.750
and then he brings you up.

00:31:25.750 --> 00:31:28.950
Well, first he sort of told
people what you were doing.

00:31:28.950 --> 00:31:30.200
But you know what, I'll
just tee it up to you.

00:31:30.200 --> 00:31:31.960
I'll just let you tell the whole story.

00:31:31.960 --> 00:31:32.880
What's that morning like?

00:31:32.880 --> 00:31:34.770
Did you know you were
going to the Rose Garden?

00:31:34.770 --> 00:31:37.520
- I wanna bring everybody back here.

00:31:37.520 --> 00:31:38.353
I wanna bring it back in time.

00:31:38.353 --> 00:31:42.520
You have to know that the
part where I quit everything

00:31:42.520 --> 00:31:45.470
and how did I end up with me being friends

00:31:45.470 --> 00:31:47.100
with the president of the United States?

00:31:47.100 --> 00:31:50.403
I think to have that, you kinda
grasp what happened there.

00:31:51.750 --> 00:31:53.710
When I quit all my drugs and everything,

00:31:53.710 --> 00:31:56.350
by the grace of God, I had never voted,

00:31:56.350 --> 00:31:58.210
I didn't know a liberal
from a conservative.

00:31:58.210 --> 00:32:00.400
I didn't know a Democrat
from a Republican.

00:32:00.400 --> 00:32:03.600
I knew nothing, and I didn't even care.

00:32:03.600 --> 00:32:05.360
Politics didn't affect me.

00:32:05.360 --> 00:32:06.660
That's what I thought,

00:32:06.660 --> 00:32:08.720
but when I came out of crack
addiction and everything,

00:32:08.720 --> 00:32:10.830
it was like coming out of a coma.

00:32:10.830 --> 00:32:12.950
I look around and I go,
"What's going on here?"

00:32:12.950 --> 00:32:15.780
My friends are all unemployed,
they're losing their houses,

00:32:15.780 --> 00:32:17.940
I'd already lost mine.

00:32:17.940 --> 00:32:20.660
We got a president giving
money to an evil empire.

00:32:20.660 --> 00:32:24.680
We got half-time of baseball
tournaments for Little League

00:32:24.680 --> 00:32:26.730
and they're giving out
first-place trophies to everyone.

00:32:26.730 --> 00:32:29.130
I go, "What is going on?"

00:32:29.130 --> 00:32:30.890
I mean, everything had changed.

00:32:30.890 --> 00:32:32.480
I'm going, "This is crazy."

00:32:32.480 --> 00:32:36.760
Well, anyway, then you get up to 2016,

00:32:36.760 --> 00:32:38.300
I explain a lot more in my book,

00:32:38.300 --> 00:32:42.750
but I get invited by Donald
Trump before he was president

00:32:42.750 --> 00:32:46.860
to come to New York City to Trump Tower.

00:32:46.860 --> 00:32:51.380
I get there, a private
meeting, on August 15, 2016.

00:32:51.380 --> 00:32:53.257
Now, I walk in there and
it was just him and I,

00:32:53.257 --> 00:32:55.063
and he goes, "Mike, do you
always wear your cross?"

00:32:55.063 --> 00:32:57.817
I go, "Yeah, Mr. Trump, this
is a divine appointment."

00:32:57.817 --> 00:33:00.013
And for some reason, I wasn't nervous.

00:33:01.217 --> 00:33:03.290
I go, "Wow, he's a normal guy."

00:33:03.290 --> 00:33:06.520
And he started telling me
all these things about...

00:33:06.520 --> 00:33:07.527
They had told me, "Whatever you do,

00:33:07.527 --> 00:33:09.490
"don't tell him you're
an ex-crack addict."

00:33:09.490 --> 00:33:10.807
That's one of the first things I told him,

00:33:10.807 --> 00:33:12.630
"And by the way, I was
an ex-crack addict,"

00:33:12.630 --> 00:33:15.690
and I got him when he had
big platform for addiction.

00:33:15.690 --> 00:33:17.427
And he goes, "I wanna wipe out the drugs.

00:33:17.427 --> 00:33:19.380
"I wanna build a wall,
they're pouring in."

00:33:19.380 --> 00:33:21.520
He told me about how he
wanted to bring jobs back

00:33:21.520 --> 00:33:25.350
and manufacturing back here
to the U.S., like MyPillow.

00:33:25.350 --> 00:33:27.010
And he asked me questions about that.

00:33:27.010 --> 00:33:29.587
I mean, I'm going, "This
guy, wow, he really cares.

00:33:29.587 --> 00:33:32.310
"He has no agenda other than
he cares about our country."

00:33:32.310 --> 00:33:35.530
I had been everywhere from
people who eat with four forks

00:33:35.530 --> 00:33:37.920
to no forks, and I'll tell
you one thing I learned

00:33:37.920 --> 00:33:39.660
in all those years of being in that bar.

00:33:39.660 --> 00:33:42.120
I could judge character,
and I'm telling you,

00:33:42.120 --> 00:33:45.960
he was just genuine, it was amazing.

00:33:45.960 --> 00:33:48.430
I walked outta there a half hour later,

00:33:48.430 --> 00:33:51.650
and I go, "He's gonna be the
greatest president in history."

00:33:51.650 --> 00:33:53.830
I went to his employees
'cause I couldn't believe

00:33:53.830 --> 00:33:56.500
what I'd just seen, talked
to so many of employees.

00:33:56.500 --> 00:33:58.140
I want everyone to listen to that.

00:33:58.140 --> 00:34:00.373
Every one of them said great things.

00:34:00.373 --> 00:34:01.410
I go, "Is this real?"

00:34:01.410 --> 00:34:02.707
He goes, "Oh, he's the best boss.

00:34:02.707 --> 00:34:05.240
"He helped me out personally."

00:34:05.240 --> 00:34:08.880
It was every one, same thing, same thing,

00:34:08.880 --> 00:34:11.140
from a doorman to a
clerk, it didn't matter.

00:34:11.140 --> 00:34:13.690
Now I go back, and I want
everyone to hear this,

00:34:13.690 --> 00:34:17.880
I go back to Minnesota
and I tell my board,

00:34:17.880 --> 00:34:19.680
I said, "You guys,"

00:34:19.680 --> 00:34:22.220
this was right in the
heat of the campaign,

00:34:22.220 --> 00:34:25.440
I tell my board at MyPillow, I
said, "You won't believe it."

00:34:25.440 --> 00:34:27.507
I said, "He's gonna help this country.

00:34:27.507 --> 00:34:29.857
"I've never seen anything like
it, it's gonna be amazing.

00:34:29.857 --> 00:34:31.503
"And I wanna do a press release

00:34:31.503 --> 00:34:33.770
"and I wanna go telling people on TV."

00:34:33.770 --> 00:34:35.760
Back then, I could tell the media

00:34:35.760 --> 00:34:37.400
that I'm walking across the street,

00:34:37.400 --> 00:34:38.822
20 cameras would show up.

00:34:38.822 --> 00:34:39.690
(Dave laughing)

00:34:39.690 --> 00:34:44.110
But anyway, my board said, a
member, my corporate attorney,

00:34:44.110 --> 00:34:46.810
he goes, "If you do this,
you're gonna ruin our company."

00:34:46.810 --> 00:34:48.840
I got mad and I went outside the office,

00:34:48.840 --> 00:34:50.927
and my CMO came out and she goes,

00:34:50.927 --> 00:34:53.170
"We didn't get this far by
you not listening to God."

00:34:53.170 --> 00:34:54.090
I go, "You're right."

00:34:54.090 --> 00:34:55.537
I went back in that boardroom and I said,

00:34:55.537 --> 00:34:58.130
"We didn't get this far by
me not listening to God,"

00:34:58.130 --> 00:35:02.550
'cause I felt it was my
calling, that I had to back him,

00:35:02.550 --> 00:35:05.930
that it was something I was
divinely supposed to do.

00:35:05.930 --> 00:35:08.050
And so I did that press release.

00:35:08.050 --> 00:35:10.370
Now, I didn't even tell
them what we talked about.

00:35:10.370 --> 00:35:12.087
You would think the press would be,

00:35:12.087 --> 00:35:15.117
"Wow, a Minnesotan, just random guy

00:35:15.117 --> 00:35:17.470
"that has a great story
about being an addict,

00:35:17.470 --> 00:35:20.637
"that now he's gotten salvation,
he's gotten redemption,

00:35:20.637 --> 00:35:23.670
"and he got to meet what
could be the president."

00:35:23.670 --> 00:35:25.110
You know what?

00:35:25.110 --> 00:35:26.520
None of them called.

00:35:26.520 --> 00:35:30.090
But some of them did contact
me, they called me a racist,

00:35:30.090 --> 00:35:32.110
they called me everything
you could think of.

00:35:32.110 --> 00:35:33.950
The Better Business Bureau in Minnesota

00:35:33.950 --> 00:35:35.320
took MyPillow's rating

00:35:35.320 --> 00:35:37.683
from an A plus to an F.
- Wow.

00:35:38.660 --> 00:35:41.040
- 'Cause I ran my buy one,
get one free too long,

00:35:41.040 --> 00:35:44.640
because that's their own little internal

00:35:45.870 --> 00:35:46.993
whatever, bars.

00:35:48.683 --> 00:35:52.170
They're a pay-for-play
business, they're not a bureau.

00:35:52.170 --> 00:35:56.070
Anyway, and then the lawyers
in California tapped me.

00:35:56.070 --> 00:35:59.463
They went after me for all kinds of stuff.

00:35:59.463 --> 00:36:01.283
- Had you ever experienced
anything like that?

00:36:01.283 --> 00:36:02.640
I mean, you had had your
own trials and tribulations,

00:36:02.640 --> 00:36:04.870
but had you ever seen just by, oh,

00:36:04.870 --> 00:36:07.670
saying I'm gonna support
this guy or I like this guy,

00:36:07.670 --> 00:36:10.300
to watch like a machine go after you?

00:36:10.300 --> 00:36:11.703
- No, nothing like it.

00:36:11.703 --> 00:36:13.430
I could compare stuff back in the day.

00:36:13.430 --> 00:36:15.000
You know, I've had swords to my throat,

00:36:15.000 --> 00:36:18.690
I've had guns to my head, you
read my book, I've had it,

00:36:18.690 --> 00:36:19.890
it's all happened to me.

00:36:19.890 --> 00:36:21.737
But something like this,
where you're going,

00:36:21.737 --> 00:36:23.580
"What did I do?"

00:36:23.580 --> 00:36:25.330
It's like I couldn't believe it.

00:36:25.330 --> 00:36:28.120
And then you're trying
to destroy my dream,

00:36:28.120 --> 00:36:30.390
this dream we had gotten so big,

00:36:30.390 --> 00:36:32.863
and you're trying to destroy
it and all my employees.

00:36:32.863 --> 00:36:33.800
That was my hurt.

00:36:33.800 --> 00:36:36.240
I go, "They're gonna kill
us, all my employees."

00:36:36.240 --> 00:36:40.120
I had probably 800 employees
or 1,000 employees at the time,

00:36:40.120 --> 00:36:42.030
and they're just attacking.

00:36:42.030 --> 00:36:43.634
We were in the news.

00:36:43.634 --> 00:36:46.084
All of them would come
up, even every newscaster,

00:36:47.984 --> 00:36:50.150
when the BBB took me
from an A plus to an F,

00:36:50.150 --> 00:36:51.560
every news outlet in the country,

00:36:51.560 --> 00:36:52.780
I was the story of the year,

00:36:52.780 --> 00:36:55.960
and that was like January 2, 2017.

00:36:55.960 --> 00:36:57.650
Every news was out
there, it didn't matter,

00:36:57.650 --> 00:37:01.250
ABC, NBC, CBS, CNN, it didn't matter.

00:37:01.250 --> 00:37:03.420
And they're just slamming
me and soundbiting me

00:37:03.420 --> 00:37:04.893
and making me look terrible.

00:37:06.460 --> 00:37:08.470
So I learned fast there.

00:37:08.470 --> 00:37:10.397
Right away I said, "I'm
only doing live interviews,

00:37:10.397 --> 00:37:12.847
"'cause you're not gonna
take it and chop me up."

00:37:14.200 --> 00:37:15.200
But I've gotten used to it.

00:37:15.200 --> 00:37:19.480
I actually now, it's over,
once you get past that,

00:37:19.480 --> 00:37:20.870
it's too late to close the gate,

00:37:20.870 --> 00:37:22.330
the cows are outta the barn.

00:37:22.330 --> 00:37:25.230
I am growing stronger
and I'm not changing.

00:37:25.230 --> 00:37:26.520
You can sit there.

00:37:26.520 --> 00:37:27.750
Over the past couple of years,

00:37:27.750 --> 00:37:30.060
every time they say something wrong on Fox

00:37:30.060 --> 00:37:31.890
or do something there, or not wrong,

00:37:31.890 --> 00:37:34.250
but say something that they don't like,

00:37:34.250 --> 00:37:36.220
they'll go, "Boycott
MyPillow and Mike Lindell."

00:37:36.220 --> 00:37:38.817
That's when they say, "Don't boycott him,

00:37:38.817 --> 00:37:40.070
"he'll double his ads."

00:37:40.070 --> 00:37:42.090
Well, like I've told them before,

00:37:42.090 --> 00:37:44.950
I advertise across the
board on every station.

00:37:44.950 --> 00:37:48.080
If I had to pick and
choose what every host says

00:37:48.080 --> 00:37:52.161
on cable TV, they go, "Oh,
that's subjective there.

00:37:52.161 --> 00:37:53.277
"You know what, I'm not gonna put an ad

00:37:53.277 --> 00:37:54.720
"on you right there."

00:37:54.720 --> 00:37:58.130
I've had CNN and MSNBC
badmouth me directly,

00:37:58.130 --> 00:37:59.830
and I still advertise.

00:37:59.830 --> 00:38:01.380
I keep it separate.

00:38:01.380 --> 00:38:02.840
I enjoy the fight.
- Not only that,

00:38:02.840 --> 00:38:06.220
you've also doubled down
when boycotts have come on

00:38:06.220 --> 00:38:07.730
for certain hosts, right?

00:38:07.730 --> 00:38:09.350
When they were really going after Tucker,

00:38:09.350 --> 00:38:11.530
weren't you the one that filled the gap?

00:38:11.530 --> 00:38:12.363
- Filled it up.

00:38:12.363 --> 00:38:14.980
Back with Laura Ingraham,
she was the first

00:38:14.980 --> 00:38:18.370
big boycott that they
did, and we ran my ad

00:38:18.370 --> 00:38:19.487
right at the start of the hour

00:38:19.487 --> 00:38:21.830
and I just filled it up with MyPillow ads.

00:38:21.830 --> 00:38:24.180
I was the only one
basically for a while there,

00:38:25.350 --> 00:38:29.400
because I couldn't believe
it, what they were doing.

00:38:29.400 --> 00:38:32.250
You're trying to tell me and
you're telling my employees,

00:38:33.420 --> 00:38:34.253
let me see...

00:38:34.253 --> 00:38:37.383
You never see their faces
either, the hidden ones,

00:38:39.280 --> 00:38:41.240
other than hosts that'll say stuff.

00:38:41.240 --> 00:38:43.610
But here's what happened though last week.

00:38:43.610 --> 00:38:45.270
So we got a little rerun here.

00:38:45.270 --> 00:38:48.590
I never thought that my popular fame

00:38:48.590 --> 00:38:51.520
could go any bigger, whatever,

00:38:51.520 --> 00:38:53.350
infamous fame, whatever you wanna call it,

00:38:53.350 --> 00:38:55.680
but I start making masks.

00:38:55.680 --> 00:38:57.520
I converted my whole company,

00:38:57.520 --> 00:39:02.360
75% over to making cloth masks,
and it was quite a project.

00:39:02.360 --> 00:39:03.910
We had to train all the employees,

00:39:03.910 --> 00:39:05.770
but we did it in like four days.

00:39:05.770 --> 00:39:07.507
- Can you just explain a little
bit about how you do that?

00:39:07.507 --> 00:39:11.740
Did you have to bring in
experts to change machines?

00:39:11.740 --> 00:39:12.670
- I made a call.

00:39:12.670 --> 00:39:14.730
I made a call to the
vice president's office,

00:39:14.730 --> 00:39:17.250
actually an email, and
they sent me right away

00:39:17.250 --> 00:39:20.600
to Peter Navarro and
whatever he was running,

00:39:20.600 --> 00:39:22.180
and I didn't know who Peter Navarro was,

00:39:22.180 --> 00:39:24.200
and then he emailed me right back,

00:39:24.200 --> 00:39:26.887
and he directed me to a task
force they had already set up

00:39:26.887 --> 00:39:29.727
and a little coalition
about anybody that was...

00:39:29.727 --> 00:39:31.980
All these different
things, from masks to gowns

00:39:31.980 --> 00:39:33.920
or whatever, kinda like let's set this up

00:39:33.920 --> 00:39:36.380
so people can have their
questions answered.

00:39:36.380 --> 00:39:38.938
So I called them and the
first question, I said,

00:39:38.938 --> 00:39:40.227
"What are the measurements?

00:39:40.227 --> 00:39:42.480
"Is there a restriction
that I have to know about?"

00:39:42.480 --> 00:39:44.730
'Cause obviously I have to
worry about getting sued

00:39:44.730 --> 00:39:48.190
by frivolous lawyers in
California, let's not forget that.

00:39:48.190 --> 00:39:51.650
So, I had to make sure
everything was right.

00:39:51.650 --> 00:39:54.090
In the meantime, I already
said I'm doing this,

00:39:54.090 --> 00:39:57.440
so my employees, they're
very good at scaling.

00:39:57.440 --> 00:40:00.030
I've had some of the same
team, we're like a big family.

00:40:00.030 --> 00:40:01.140
We just started going.

00:40:01.140 --> 00:40:03.190
We took the sewing machines, moved them,

00:40:03.190 --> 00:40:05.290
made them eight feet apart.

00:40:05.290 --> 00:40:08.203
We had to move racking.

00:40:09.334 --> 00:40:11.570
Then I had to make sure that
we had the right fabric.

00:40:11.570 --> 00:40:15.080
It was a blessing, the MyPillow
fabric was perfect for it.

00:40:15.080 --> 00:40:17.250
We just had to not do two processes,

00:40:17.250 --> 00:40:18.520
printing and another thing.

00:40:18.520 --> 00:40:20.100
So we had to do a different process,

00:40:20.100 --> 00:40:21.980
but it wasn't a big switch.

00:40:21.980 --> 00:40:23.490
And then I had to get elastic.

00:40:23.490 --> 00:40:24.580
At first, I bought the wrong elastic.

00:40:24.580 --> 00:40:28.220
It had latex, so I had to dump
that, get the right elastic.

00:40:28.220 --> 00:40:29.950
There was a little shortage for one day,

00:40:29.950 --> 00:40:32.140
but I was determined I was gonna get it.

00:40:32.140 --> 00:40:35.710
And then we had a really
expensive cutting machine

00:40:35.710 --> 00:40:37.590
so we could cut the patterns.

00:40:37.590 --> 00:40:40.250
And we were up and making
masks in three days.

00:40:40.250 --> 00:40:42.532
Everyone was trained.
- Incredible.

00:40:42.532 --> 00:40:45.173
I think we made close
to 10,000 the first day.

00:40:46.630 --> 00:40:48.320
We added two shifts.

00:40:48.320 --> 00:40:50.360
A friend of mine, 'cause a lot
of them had to be laundered

00:40:50.360 --> 00:40:51.860
at a commercial laundromat.

00:40:51.860 --> 00:40:54.600
I was up till 12 every day
setting the foundation,

00:40:54.600 --> 00:40:57.170
till midnight, starting
again at five in the morning.

00:40:57.170 --> 00:41:00.520
Well, then I get an email from
the vice president's office

00:41:00.520 --> 00:41:02.290
and said, "Could you come out

00:41:03.609 --> 00:41:05.600
"and be involved in a roundtable?"

00:41:05.600 --> 00:41:08.290
I was involved in one in 2017,

00:41:08.290 --> 00:41:10.040
first time I was ever in the White House,

00:41:10.040 --> 00:41:12.120
and for Made in America.

00:41:12.120 --> 00:41:15.440
And they said, "And we'd like
you to write some remarks."

00:41:15.440 --> 00:41:18.360
And I'm going, okay,
they gotta get approved.

00:41:18.360 --> 00:41:19.487
I'm going, "What do I need remarks

00:41:19.487 --> 00:41:20.790
"for a roundtable for?"

00:41:20.790 --> 00:41:22.890
So actually, the remarks are here.

00:41:22.890 --> 00:41:24.540
These are the typed ones here.

00:41:24.540 --> 00:41:26.550
These are the typed remarks, okay?

00:41:26.550 --> 00:41:28.347
So I type them up and send them out there,

00:41:28.347 --> 00:41:30.080
and I wasn't even real particular.

00:41:30.080 --> 00:41:32.280
They wanted remarks of what we were doing

00:41:32.280 --> 00:41:35.800
and specifically about
what MyPillow was doing.

00:41:35.800 --> 00:41:37.540
I'm going, okay, I don't really...

00:41:37.540 --> 00:41:39.400
That's fine, I don't
really need to brag about

00:41:39.400 --> 00:41:42.556
what I'm doing to help the
country, but I'll do it,

00:41:42.556 --> 00:41:44.690
it sits in a roundtable.

00:41:44.690 --> 00:41:47.810
So I fly out there, we
get to the roundtable

00:41:47.810 --> 00:41:50.780
and all the five CEOs that are there,

00:41:50.780 --> 00:41:53.850
the vice president, a
couple guys down at the end,

00:41:53.850 --> 00:41:56.870
I forget who they were,
and we go around the table

00:41:56.870 --> 00:41:59.480
and each one, well, this
one's doing respirators

00:41:59.480 --> 00:42:01.700
and this one, I said, "We're doing masks."

00:42:01.700 --> 00:42:03.950
But I wasn't looking, nobody
was looking at their remarks

00:42:03.950 --> 00:42:06.653
or whatever, I didn't
even seen any papers out.

00:42:07.742 --> 00:42:10.250
So then the president came in
and it was a good half hour

00:42:10.250 --> 00:42:11.770
of everyone saying what they're doing.

00:42:11.770 --> 00:42:13.803
You guys, can you make more?

00:42:15.250 --> 00:42:16.293
What are your plans?

00:42:17.260 --> 00:42:20.121
We get done, and the president
gets up and they all get up,

00:42:20.121 --> 00:42:21.627
and I said to the vice president, I said,

00:42:21.627 --> 00:42:22.810
"We didn't read our remarks."

00:42:22.810 --> 00:42:24.607
He goes, "Oh, no, no,
they're for our outside.

00:42:24.607 --> 00:42:26.333
"The president might call
you up to the thing."

00:42:26.333 --> 00:42:28.190
And I go, "Really?"

00:42:28.190 --> 00:42:31.950
So now, we go into the other
room towards the Oval Office

00:42:31.950 --> 00:42:35.210
and the president, he was
showing the other CEOs,

00:42:35.210 --> 00:42:37.210
kinda giving a little mini tour here,

00:42:37.210 --> 00:42:39.210
and then he sits down and
he's gotta read his speech

00:42:39.210 --> 00:42:40.550
with the vice president.

00:42:40.550 --> 00:42:42.900
And we're sitting over
there at this table,

00:42:42.900 --> 00:42:45.327
and I thought, you know
what, I'm reading the remarks

00:42:45.327 --> 00:42:46.290
and I go, you know what,

00:42:46.290 --> 00:42:49.130
I wanted to give a message
of hope to the people.

00:42:49.130 --> 00:42:51.440
So I start writing on the back,

00:42:51.440 --> 00:42:53.720
and if you can see my scribbles,

00:42:53.720 --> 00:42:56.601
there's little arrows
that go down and stuff,

00:42:56.601 --> 00:42:58.520
and when I wrote it, I
thought I would rewrite it

00:42:58.520 --> 00:43:00.090
on a clean piece of paper.

00:43:00.090 --> 00:43:02.200
I just get done with the last thing,

00:43:02.200 --> 00:43:04.160
I mean, there's crossed
out and everything,

00:43:04.160 --> 00:43:06.783
and they go, "Okay, we're
going out to the Rose Garden,"

00:43:06.783 --> 00:43:08.080
and I'm going, "What?"

00:43:08.080 --> 00:43:10.827
I'm going, okay, so all I said was,

00:43:10.827 --> 00:43:13.280
"God, please let me read my writing."

00:43:13.280 --> 00:43:15.670
(laughing)

00:43:15.670 --> 00:43:19.280
It turned out the president
calls me up first.

00:43:19.280 --> 00:43:21.080
I came right up, we didn't practice this,

00:43:21.080 --> 00:43:23.440
so I didn't know we were
all gonna go around the end,

00:43:23.440 --> 00:43:25.620
so he called me up first,
and I went straight up,

00:43:25.620 --> 00:43:27.840
so I think they held the other CEOs back

00:43:27.840 --> 00:43:29.620
so it was just him and I.

00:43:29.620 --> 00:43:33.990
And here's a guy that has so
much nervousness of speaking,

00:43:33.990 --> 00:43:37.960
now I did, my throat, I
had vocal cord surgery

00:43:37.960 --> 00:43:41.703
just a week before, so I was
a little raspy like I am now,

00:43:43.040 --> 00:43:44.420
and I get up there and I read them,

00:43:44.420 --> 00:43:48.267
and then I just felt led, and
I turned around and I said,

00:43:48.267 --> 00:43:49.107
"Mr. President, do you mind

00:43:49.107 --> 00:43:50.910
"if I read something off the cuff now?"

00:43:50.910 --> 00:43:52.470
He said, "Yes."

00:43:52.470 --> 00:43:56.393
And then I read that God gave
us grace on November 8, 2016,

00:43:59.495 --> 00:44:01.300
and just read that and talked about

00:44:01.300 --> 00:44:04.310
that the nation had turned its back on God

00:44:04.310 --> 00:44:07.490
and we should spend this
time reading the Bibles,

00:44:07.490 --> 00:44:08.470
getting back in the Word,

00:44:08.470 --> 00:44:10.570
and spending time with our families.

00:44:10.570 --> 00:44:12.647
And I said, "We're all
gonna get through this

00:44:12.647 --> 00:44:15.597
"with this great administration
and everybody's prayers,

00:44:15.597 --> 00:44:17.867
"and everybody combined, and
we're all in this together,

00:44:17.867 --> 00:44:20.630
"and we're gonna be stronger
and safer than ever."

00:44:20.630 --> 00:44:22.857
You have have think I'd shot somebody.

00:44:22.857 --> 00:44:24.988
(laughing)

00:44:24.988 --> 00:44:29.840
- Okay, so you do all
this, it's impromptu,

00:44:29.840 --> 00:44:33.180
he's letting you do your
thing, you talk about God,

00:44:33.180 --> 00:44:35.030
you're making I think at one point,

00:44:35.030 --> 00:44:37.823
you were making 50,000 masks a day, right?

00:44:39.290 --> 00:44:41.270
Yeah, you're doing that right now.

00:44:41.270 --> 00:44:45.400
So you finish the speech, and
did you even think about it

00:44:45.400 --> 00:44:47.800
or realize what was
about to come your way?

00:44:47.800 --> 00:44:49.540
Did it even cross your mind?

00:44:49.540 --> 00:44:51.960
- No, do you know what, it was like to me

00:44:51.960 --> 00:44:53.060
it didn't feel like...

00:44:54.110 --> 00:44:57.200
I didn't think it'd be a
shot heard round the world.

00:44:57.200 --> 00:44:59.630
We went back into the White House,

00:44:59.630 --> 00:45:02.330
and the first inkling I got
that it might be real big

00:45:02.330 --> 00:45:05.490
was the vice president
came to me, and he goes,

00:45:05.490 --> 00:45:07.710
he was just, "Wow, Mike."

00:45:07.710 --> 00:45:10.267
He goes, "You've opened up the heavens.

00:45:10.267 --> 00:45:12.760
"I mean, people are gonna, you're just..."

00:45:12.760 --> 00:45:14.040
I don't even remember what he said,

00:45:14.040 --> 00:45:16.720
but I could just tell he just loved it.

00:45:16.720 --> 00:45:18.440
I'm going, good, I got
a little confirmation

00:45:18.440 --> 00:45:19.860
that it was okay.

00:45:19.860 --> 00:45:22.140
The president never said a thing about it.

00:45:22.140 --> 00:45:24.123
He was talking to the CEOs and us.

00:45:26.830 --> 00:45:29.750
When I left the White House, I finally,

00:45:29.750 --> 00:45:33.548
you got my phone back, see
they have your phones, right?

00:45:33.548 --> 00:45:36.690
And I open up my phone and turn it on,

00:45:36.690 --> 00:45:41.190
I had 750 text messages.

00:45:41.190 --> 00:45:44.340
I didn't know that many
people had my phone number.

00:45:44.340 --> 00:45:45.173
- Dear God.
- And I'm going,

00:45:45.173 --> 00:45:46.006
"What had happened?"

00:45:46.006 --> 00:45:48.720
I looked at Twitter and it
was just (robotic whirring).

00:45:49.650 --> 00:45:52.290
I looked at my Facebook, it had blown up.

00:45:52.290 --> 00:45:56.043
I had 2,000 emails, and
I'm trying to drive,

00:45:56.043 --> 00:45:58.453
and I'm going, wow, I had to pull over.

00:45:59.546 --> 00:46:00.850
I'm calling friends,
I go, "What happened?"

00:46:00.850 --> 00:46:03.107
They go, "Don't you know,
everybody's talking about it."

00:46:03.107 --> 00:46:04.867
And I'm going, "Really?"

00:46:05.880 --> 00:46:09.450
So from that point, I've
done 80 some interviews

00:46:09.450 --> 00:46:12.040
as of today, every day, all day.

00:46:12.040 --> 00:46:14.580
I've gotten calls from Israel,

00:46:14.580 --> 00:46:16.270
my friends in Australia,

00:46:16.270 --> 00:46:18.550
they said it was on top of all the news.

00:46:18.550 --> 00:46:20.430
In the Taiwan paper, it was the cover

00:46:20.430 --> 00:46:21.860
of their national paper.

00:46:21.860 --> 00:46:23.650
This was like you'd think it was...

00:46:24.530 --> 00:46:25.510
One of the good things there

00:46:25.510 --> 00:46:27.490
is I'm glad I asked the president,

00:46:27.490 --> 00:46:30.870
because everybody knew he had no idea.

00:46:30.870 --> 00:46:33.917
He had no idea, so people that said,

00:46:33.917 --> 00:46:35.647
"Oh, you're mixing church and state,

00:46:35.647 --> 00:46:39.780
"or church and God, or whatever,
God and the government,"

00:46:39.780 --> 00:46:42.270
you know what, I did that,
so what are you gonna do,

00:46:42.270 --> 00:46:44.180
put me in jail, sorry.

00:46:44.180 --> 00:46:47.730
- Right, well, the government
didn't force anyone

00:46:47.730 --> 00:46:48.640
to listen to you.

00:46:48.640 --> 00:46:51.810
People could either hear you and believe

00:46:51.810 --> 00:46:54.033
or enjoy what you say, or not, so be it.

00:46:55.020 --> 00:46:57.530
Okay, but now talk about
just the media reaction,

00:46:57.530 --> 00:46:59.370
'cause I'm sure you're
getting a lotta love

00:46:59.370 --> 00:47:01.210
from nice quarters, and it must be nice

00:47:01.210 --> 00:47:03.120
to hear the vice president
say some nice things,

00:47:03.120 --> 00:47:06.220
but really, I was watching
it as it happened on Twitter,

00:47:06.220 --> 00:47:11.120
and the amount of mainstream media people,

00:47:11.120 --> 00:47:15.350
who've never donated a dollar,
given up any of their time,

00:47:15.350 --> 00:47:18.610
they're, "Oh, the MyPillow
guy," mocking you,

00:47:18.610 --> 00:47:19.707
mocking Trump for bringing you on,

00:47:19.707 --> 00:47:21.550
it's a big stunt, blah blah blah.

00:47:21.550 --> 00:47:23.940
Meanwhile, you're the
one, I mean, it cost you,

00:47:23.940 --> 00:47:24.940
you don't have to tell me how much,

00:47:24.940 --> 00:47:26.980
but I assume it cost you quite a penny

00:47:26.980 --> 00:47:29.090
to convert the operation.

00:47:29.090 --> 00:47:31.990
Not only that, but what you're
then not making in pillows,

00:47:32.874 --> 00:47:34.603
and the rest of it.
- Oh, absolutely.

00:47:34.603 --> 00:47:37.670
That was God's way of rewarding me

00:47:37.670 --> 00:47:39.600
for just speaking out his name,

00:47:39.600 --> 00:47:42.783
because now when that happened, everybody,

00:47:43.840 --> 00:47:45.270
we had laid off a bunch of people

00:47:45.270 --> 00:47:46.810
that were on the road doing home shows.

00:47:46.810 --> 00:47:49.420
I have 90 some people that
do home shows and fairs,

00:47:49.420 --> 00:47:52.550
like I used to do, they
had lost their jobs

00:47:52.550 --> 00:47:54.850
because they're closed
and my stores were closed.

00:47:54.850 --> 00:47:56.011
Well, now they could all get,

00:47:56.011 --> 00:47:57.900
(phone ringing)
they could all get on phones.

00:47:57.900 --> 00:47:59.110
- The calls are still coming in.

00:47:59.110 --> 00:48:01.052
- [Dave] Yeah, they're still coming in.

00:48:01.052 --> 00:48:02.850
(laughing)

00:48:02.850 --> 00:48:06.080
But they could get on phones
now and our business went up.

00:48:06.080 --> 00:48:08.640
Like you say, for every one attack,

00:48:08.640 --> 00:48:10.650
nine people, it's even more than that.

00:48:10.650 --> 00:48:12.680
I think for every one attack,

00:48:12.680 --> 00:48:14.980
50 people would go after that guy.

00:48:14.980 --> 00:48:16.530
What's wrong with you?

00:48:16.530 --> 00:48:18.090
They would tell that guy,
"What is wrong with you?

00:48:18.090 --> 00:48:19.657
"He's doing great things.

00:48:19.657 --> 00:48:20.850
"What have you done?"

00:48:20.850 --> 00:48:22.540
And these hosts on MSN...

00:48:22.540 --> 00:48:25.360
Jim Acosta was sitting 10 feet from me,

00:48:25.360 --> 00:48:29.970
and he badmouthed me saying
it was a PR stunt that I did.

00:48:29.970 --> 00:48:32.090
He blamed me directly,

00:48:32.090 --> 00:48:34.760
a PR stunt to get to promote MyPillow.

00:48:34.760 --> 00:48:35.660
Are you kidding?

00:48:35.660 --> 00:48:37.620
Maybe you didn't listen right, Jim.

00:48:37.620 --> 00:48:40.810
I was promoting Jesus,
I was promoting Bibles,

00:48:40.810 --> 00:48:42.850
and spending time with our families.

00:48:42.850 --> 00:48:44.480
He got it a little wrong there.

00:48:44.480 --> 00:48:45.980
Maybe he didn't listen.

00:48:45.980 --> 00:48:48.110
Maybe he only listened to
the first part of the speech,

00:48:48.110 --> 00:48:50.600
which every CEO went up
there and talked about

00:48:50.600 --> 00:48:52.300
what they were doing for the country,

00:48:52.300 --> 00:48:53.630
and Jim, what are you doing?

00:48:53.630 --> 00:48:55.723
These were the things that was like...

00:48:55.723 --> 00:48:57.880
And then I went on all this media,

00:48:57.880 --> 00:49:00.880
but it was a good thing because
I was on a lot of media too,

00:49:02.870 --> 00:49:04.970
I was able to take the politics out of it,

00:49:04.970 --> 00:49:06.350
we're all in this together.

00:49:06.350 --> 00:49:09.600
I don't care if you're a
Democrat, Republican, liberal...

00:49:09.600 --> 00:49:11.790
It don't matter, I went
on all these outlets,

00:49:11.790 --> 00:49:14.960
from "People" magazine
to the "Washington Post,"

00:49:14.960 --> 00:49:16.973
Fox, I mean it didn't matter.

00:49:19.325 --> 00:49:21.540
The actual outlets treated me right.

00:49:21.540 --> 00:49:22.960
I mean, they actually treated me right.

00:49:22.960 --> 00:49:25.230
It was these hosts, late-night hosts.

00:49:25.230 --> 00:49:27.467
One late-night host said,
"We got Mike Lindell

00:49:27.467 --> 00:49:29.907
"coming on tonight from MyPillow.

00:49:29.907 --> 00:49:32.307
"He's gonna talk about
absolutely nothing."

00:49:33.429 --> 00:49:35.890
And "Saturday Night Live,"
of course, they did their...

00:49:35.890 --> 00:49:37.960
Alec Baldwin did his, the mess he is,

00:49:37.960 --> 00:49:41.323
he did his mocking.

00:49:43.500 --> 00:49:47.870
So what I say is this, and
I told the president this,

00:49:47.870 --> 00:49:48.870
I did tell him this.

00:49:48.870 --> 00:49:50.290
I said, "You know, Mr. President,"

00:49:50.290 --> 00:49:52.657
I said, "these press
releases that you're doing,

00:49:52.657 --> 00:49:54.570
"or these press conferences,"

00:49:54.570 --> 00:49:58.400
I said, "people are seeing
how a great leader you are."

00:49:58.400 --> 00:50:00.380
His ratings up 60 some percent.

00:50:00.380 --> 00:50:02.440
But I said, "I wanna read you something."

00:50:02.440 --> 00:50:04.157
I said, "This guy is a friend of mine

00:50:04.157 --> 00:50:05.690
"and I've known him all my life,"

00:50:05.690 --> 00:50:08.410
and I said, "he sent me
this text, and it said,

00:50:08.410 --> 00:50:11.910
Mike, you know I'm not a
big President Trump fan,"

00:50:11.910 --> 00:50:14.030
he's a never-Trumper is what he is.

00:50:14.030 --> 00:50:16.547
He said, "But you know
what, God bless him.

00:50:16.547 --> 00:50:18.477
"He's doing a champion of a job.

00:50:18.477 --> 00:50:20.300
"I think he's turning me."

00:50:20.300 --> 00:50:23.850
And you know what, what's
happening is the whole country

00:50:25.240 --> 00:50:28.210
is coming on board and they're gonna see

00:50:28.210 --> 00:50:31.260
that having a pragmatic,
common-sense president,

00:50:31.260 --> 00:50:34.400
who's an information vacuum
cleaner takes it all in.

00:50:34.400 --> 00:50:36.290
What other president would take and listen

00:50:36.290 --> 00:50:40.330
to private sector people,
listen to his governors,

00:50:40.330 --> 00:50:42.723
listen to everyone,
before he makes decisions.

00:50:44.776 --> 00:50:46.670
It's amazing having a businessman.

00:50:46.670 --> 00:50:48.370
I don't call it the Republican Party.

00:50:48.370 --> 00:50:51.550
He's changed it to the commonsense party.

00:50:51.550 --> 00:50:53.880
If I had to look at
politics before he took in,

00:50:53.880 --> 00:50:55.630
there's things in that
party I didn't like.

00:50:55.630 --> 00:50:56.850
He's divined a whole thing,

00:50:56.850 --> 00:50:59.200
this is the way it should
be, for the people.

00:50:59.200 --> 00:51:01.410
And I wanna tell everyone out there, too,

00:51:01.410 --> 00:51:05.220
that when I left the
White House that night,

00:51:05.220 --> 00:51:06.560
I had more...

00:51:06.560 --> 00:51:08.890
I'm an optimist like you wouldn't believe,

00:51:08.890 --> 00:51:12.520
but I'll tell you what, it
went from here, level two,

00:51:12.520 --> 00:51:14.930
to level 10, the highest it could be,

00:51:14.930 --> 00:51:17.160
because you know what, I
was seeing the same thing

00:51:17.160 --> 00:51:20.723
I've seen before, he was
making a decision here.

00:51:21.600 --> 00:51:23.660
Some governor, it would
have took him six months

00:51:23.660 --> 00:51:25.780
to do something, he did it in four days.

00:51:25.780 --> 00:51:26.807
He said, "Let me take care of that,

00:51:26.807 --> 00:51:27.990
"let me take care of that."

00:51:27.990 --> 00:51:31.180
We have somebody that's making decisions

00:51:31.180 --> 00:51:33.710
not based on politics.

00:51:33.710 --> 00:51:35.947
He's in the back there, he
goes, "We need to save lives,

00:51:35.947 --> 00:51:37.613
"but we need to get people back."

00:51:37.613 --> 00:51:40.340
It's the biggest decision, he
said it the other night, ever.

00:51:40.340 --> 00:51:42.880
Well, you know what, you gotta know this,

00:51:42.880 --> 00:51:45.100
every politician, and
most of them I've met,

00:51:45.100 --> 00:51:46.780
and I've met them on both sides,

00:51:46.780 --> 00:51:48.760
these career ones that are out there,

00:51:48.760 --> 00:51:50.850
they've all their lives
they've made decisions

00:51:50.850 --> 00:51:52.237
with their own agenda it seems like,

00:51:52.237 --> 00:51:54.460
and they don't have the people's back.

00:51:54.460 --> 00:51:56.330
And finally, this is what's changed.

00:51:56.330 --> 00:51:57.810
And even people on the left,

00:51:57.810 --> 00:52:01.270
I don't care if you're a
liberal or whatever you are,

00:52:01.270 --> 00:52:03.660
you're seeing that this
is the commonsense thing,

00:52:03.660 --> 00:52:06.950
because this president
knows problem/solution,

00:52:06.950 --> 00:52:08.710
but he's got a God-given talent

00:52:08.710 --> 00:52:10.920
to know what it's gonna manifest to,

00:52:10.920 --> 00:52:13.241
to help each and every one of us

00:52:13.241 --> 00:52:16.240
bring joy to our daily lives, that's it.

00:52:16.240 --> 00:52:19.840
- So as a guy that went
from an optimist to now,

00:52:19.840 --> 00:52:20.960
you can call it a super optimist,

00:52:20.960 --> 00:52:22.590
in the midst of a this craziness,

00:52:22.590 --> 00:52:25.130
and clearly you're loving life right now

00:52:25.130 --> 00:52:27.490
and things are good and you're
still producing the masks,

00:52:27.490 --> 00:52:30.390
as you just said, you had
a certain luxury in that,

00:52:30.390 --> 00:52:32.560
because you're successful,

00:52:32.560 --> 00:52:34.490
and not that they couldn't
have taken you down,

00:52:34.490 --> 00:52:37.640
but you had a bit of a cushion
there to weather a storm.

00:52:37.640 --> 00:52:39.630
What would you say, 'cause I
get this question all the time,

00:52:39.630 --> 00:52:41.270
I get this from college students,

00:52:41.270 --> 00:52:43.740
that they're afraid if they say one thing

00:52:43.740 --> 00:52:45.780
that goes against what mainstream wants,

00:52:45.780 --> 00:52:47.080
that they are gonna get destroyed,

00:52:47.080 --> 00:52:48.840
what would you say to a young person

00:52:48.840 --> 00:52:52.580
that wants to stand up, but
doesn't have that cushion

00:52:52.580 --> 00:52:55.550
or even a family that's gonna defend them

00:52:55.550 --> 00:52:57.100
or worry that they're gonna lose their job

00:52:57.100 --> 00:52:58.370
or the rest of it?

00:52:58.370 --> 00:53:00.300
- Well, you know what,
we're getting through that.

00:53:00.300 --> 00:53:03.207
If I just gave you advice
three and a half years ago,

00:53:03.207 --> 00:53:04.390
I would have said, you know what,

00:53:04.390 --> 00:53:05.650
if I'm you, I'm scared, too.

00:53:05.650 --> 00:53:08.030
I'm me, and I don't ever
back down and stuff.

00:53:08.030 --> 00:53:11.530
But not I say, you know what,
it's happening all around you.

00:53:11.530 --> 00:53:14.670
Now they're the small voice.

00:53:14.670 --> 00:53:17.300
We have to all rise up and be that voice.

00:53:17.300 --> 00:53:19.660
You speak out, your
business will be busier

00:53:19.660 --> 00:53:21.610
if you speak out for what you believe,

00:53:21.610 --> 00:53:23.843
and you don't back down to evil.

00:53:26.450 --> 00:53:27.950
And you know what, when I said that,

00:53:27.950 --> 00:53:30.870
about God being taken out
of our schools and colleges,

00:53:30.870 --> 00:53:32.240
I meant that.

00:53:32.240 --> 00:53:34.530
These young people are looking for hope.

00:53:34.530 --> 00:53:37.550
Right now is the time of the
greatest revival in history.

00:53:37.550 --> 00:53:39.630
We have people out there looking for hope,

00:53:39.630 --> 00:53:41.750
looking for something to grasp onto.

00:53:41.750 --> 00:53:42.920
What's wrong with Jesus?

00:53:42.920 --> 00:53:44.120
What's wrong with faith?

00:53:45.541 --> 00:53:46.910
And if you're an addict
and you're at home,

00:53:46.910 --> 00:53:47.920
I wanna bring this in, too,

00:53:47.920 --> 00:53:51.430
because that's what my
book is with my addiction,

00:53:51.430 --> 00:53:54.230
if you're an addict and
you're at home right now

00:53:54.230 --> 00:53:55.520
and you can't even get out, whatever,

00:53:55.520 --> 00:53:57.900
you're in quarantine or whatever it is,

00:53:57.900 --> 00:54:01.600
you know what, everybody knows before this

00:54:01.600 --> 00:54:04.243
massive deaths we were having from heroin

00:54:05.096 --> 00:54:07.343
and from fentanyl and
stuff, it's horrific.

00:54:09.310 --> 00:54:11.090
But you know what, we all know that.

00:54:11.090 --> 00:54:13.700
Now if you're a 22-year-old
opiate addict or heroin addict,

00:54:13.700 --> 00:54:15.100
you also know one of your friends

00:54:15.100 --> 00:54:16.650
that made it through your own age,

00:54:16.650 --> 00:54:19.440
just like I told you about my
friend, Dick, that came to me.

00:54:19.440 --> 00:54:21.210
Now's the time to pick up that phone

00:54:21.210 --> 00:54:23.520
while you're sitting there
and reach out to that guy,

00:54:23.520 --> 00:54:25.377
and say, "You know what,
how'd you get through?

00:54:25.377 --> 00:54:26.460
"How'd you make it?"

00:54:26.460 --> 00:54:27.940
Ask him those questions you can't get

00:54:27.940 --> 00:54:30.670
in a treatment center,
ask him the questions.

00:54:30.670 --> 00:54:32.290
That's who you need counseling you.

00:54:32.290 --> 00:54:35.450
And on the opposite end, if
you're somebody sitting at home

00:54:35.450 --> 00:54:38.130
that's made it through,
had your hearts restored,

00:54:38.130 --> 00:54:40.350
you probably went to a
Salvation Army, Teen Challenge,

00:54:40.350 --> 00:54:43.350
Union Gospel, a faith-based
treatment center that works.

00:54:43.350 --> 00:54:45.440
The secular ones' success rate,

00:54:45.440 --> 00:54:47.020
I don't even wanna get into it.

00:54:47.020 --> 00:54:48.590
They're just to take our insurance money,

00:54:48.590 --> 00:54:50.160
and it's horrible.

00:54:50.160 --> 00:54:53.450
But anyway, if you're someone
that's made it though,

00:54:53.450 --> 00:54:56.140
now's the time to reach
out to people you know

00:54:57.388 --> 00:54:59.850
that haven't made it yet,
they're still on drugs,

00:54:59.850 --> 00:55:01.530
they still need their hearts restored.

00:55:01.530 --> 00:55:03.710
They have wounds, maybe
they were fatherless

00:55:03.710 --> 00:55:06.100
or went through a divorce
or never had a father,

00:55:06.100 --> 00:55:08.430
like affected me in my life.

00:55:08.430 --> 00:55:12.190
Addiction comes from
childhood fatherlessness,

00:55:12.190 --> 00:55:13.720
wounds, trauma.

00:55:13.720 --> 00:55:16.170
Anyone that tells me,
"Oh, it's a disease,"

00:55:16.170 --> 00:55:17.150
I don't believe it.

00:55:17.150 --> 00:55:19.590
I've seen it too many
times where this happens

00:55:19.590 --> 00:55:23.170
and it manifested into using
an addiction to mask pain.

00:55:23.170 --> 00:55:25.010
Reach out to those people,

00:55:25.010 --> 00:55:27.520
and we'll make it the biggest AA meeting

00:55:27.520 --> 00:55:29.670
in the history of the United States,

00:55:29.670 --> 00:55:31.800
only we'll use Jesus as our higher power,

00:55:31.800 --> 00:55:34.060
not just some made up higher power,

00:55:34.060 --> 00:55:36.000
and it'll be amazing.

00:55:36.000 --> 00:55:37.980
This is what I want everybody to know.

00:55:37.980 --> 00:55:40.480
We're gonna get through this,
and when we get through it,

00:55:40.480 --> 00:55:42.450
we're gonna be just like 9/11.

00:55:42.450 --> 00:55:44.700
9/11, we were safer and more secure.

00:55:44.700 --> 00:55:48.000
If 9/11 hadn't happened, it's
